{"raw": {"https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/search": {"title": "Search Page", "description": "Search Page Search Page Kiosk mode To view a full description, click on the title of the position you are interested in. You may use the Apply Now! section within the full description to submit your application and upload documents. Applications with \"See Resume\" or left blank will not be considered. Individuals who do not meet the minimum stated qualifications will not be considered. *Please note: This system has recently been updated since March 1, 2023. If you applied to a position prior to this date, you will need to create a new account. The Close Date, if listed, is an estimated date. Meredith College reserves the right to change this date by shortening it or extending it based on the applicant pool. All posted positions are accepting applications. Once a position is removed from the website, it is no longer accepting applications, including incomplete applications. If you are interested in a position, we encourage you to apply. **Please note: If a close date is listed, the position will typically be removed from the website at 11:59 PM unless otherwise noted in the posting.** Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 14 filter options found Category Adjunct (2 items) 2 Administrative / Management (3 items) 3 Clerical (2 items) 2 Coach (1 items) 1 Custodial Services (1 items) 1 Faculty (2 items) 2 Fundraising / Institutional Advancement (1 items) 1 Grounds (3 items) 3 Maintenance / Facilities (5 items) 5 Other (2 items) 2 Professional (1 items) 1 Recruitment (1 items) 1 Security (4 items) 4 Student Development (3 items) 3 Department Search departments 15 filter options found Department Academic Programs (1 items) 1 Admissions (1 items) 1 Athletics (1 items) 1 Autism Program (1 items) 1 Biological Sciences (1 items) 1 Campus Police (4 items) 4 Career Planning (1 items) 1 Facilities Services (9 items) 9 Financial Assistance (1 items) 1 Institutional Advancement (1 items) 1 Marketing (1 items) 1 Nutrition, Health & Human Performance (2 items) 2 School of Business (1 items) 1 Student Affairs (1 items) 1 Student Success (2 items) 2 Employment Type Search employment types 5 filter options found Employment Type Adjunct Instructor (2 items) 2 Administrative Faculty / Staff Full-time (1 items) 1 Faculty Full-time (2 items) 2 Staff Full-time (20 items) 20 Staff Part-time (3 items) 3 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Title Category Department Employment Type Closing date HVAC Mechanic II Maintenance / Facilities Facilities Services Staff Full-time HVAC Mechanic I Maintenance / Facilities Facilities Services Staff Full-time HVAC Technician III Maintenance / Facilities Facilities Services Staff Full-time Groundskeeper Waste Specialist Grounds Facilities Services Staff Full-time Groundskeeper Tech and Equipment Specialist Grounds Facilities Services Staff Full-time Director of the Lowery Fitness Center and Campus Recreation Administrative / Management Other Student Affairs Staff Full-time Assistant Tennis Coach, Part-time Coach Athletics Staff Part-time Senior Director of Strategic Giving Fundraising / Institutional Advancement Institutional Advancement Staff Full-time Associate Director of Student Success Student Development Student Success Staff Full-time Associate Director of Student Success and Learning Center Student Development Student Success Staff Full-time Security Officer, 3rd Shift Security Campus Police Staff Full-time Police Officer Security Campus Police Staff Full-time Office and Billing Manager (Admin II) Clerical Autism Program Staff Full-time Police Officer, Part-time Security Campus Police Staff Part-time Oct 27 2026 - 11:55pm EDT Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor - 2nd Shift Custodial Services Facilities Services Staff Full-time Assistant to the Vice President for Marketing and Communications Clerical Marketing Staff Full-time Clinical Educator in Dietetics Faculty Nutrition, Health & Human Performance Faculty Full-time Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director Faculty Nutrition, Health & Human Performance Faculty Full-time Associate Director of Admissions Recruitment Admissions Staff Full-time Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Academic Programs Adjunct Instructor Security Officer, Part-time (Flexible Schedule) Security Campus Police Staff Part-time Adjunct Instructor of Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology Adjunct Biological Sciences Adjunct Instructor Director of Career Planning Administrative / Management Student Development Career Planning Staff Full-time Groundskeeper / Irrigation Technician Grounds Facilities Services Staff Full-time Chair - School of Business Administrative / Management School of Business Administrative Faculty / Staff Full-time Maintenance Technician III Maintenance / Facilities Facilities Services Staff Full-time Maintenance Technician II Maintenance / Facilities Facilities Services Staff Full-time Assistant Director of Financial Assistance Other Professional Financial Assistance Staff Full-time Displaying all 28 entries Candidate Details"}, "https://www.meredith.edu/human-resources/applying-for-a-position/": {"title": "Applying for a Position - Meredith College", "description": "Applying for a Position - Meredith College Applying for a Position - Meredith College Human Resources / Applying for a Position Applying for a Position Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) Immigration Information About Meredith Title IX: Gender Discrimination / Sexual Violence Human Resources Staff Getting to Meredith Student Employment Employee Benefits Payroll Information It is Meredith College\u2019s policy to provide and promote equal employment opportunity to all qualified persons. This applies to all aspects of the employment relationship, including, but not limited to, recruitment, selection, advancement, compensation, benefits, discipline, training, leave, transfer and termination. Current vacancies Log in to complete/update applications vacancies The online web-based system allows you to attach resumes, cover letters or other documents to your application. You may update or edit your application for additional positions as they become available. Applications may be entered from any online computer. For your convenience, computers are available in the Office of Human Resources (Park Center, first floor), in the Carlyle Campbell Library, or the Cate Center. We do not accept paper applications for any position posted online. If you need any assistance with the application process, please contact us at jobs@meredith.edu . Your application is important to us and we will contact you as soon as possible. Additional options for assistance are available by calling (919) 760-8898. If you need accommodation(s) in the application process because of a disability, please notify the Office of Human Resources of your requirements. All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory criminal background check results. Thank you for your interest in employment with Meredith College! Current Employees: MyMeredith Portal Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/hvac-mechanic-ii-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "HVAC Mechanic II", "description": "HVAC Mechanic II - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States HVAC Mechanic II - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode HVAC Mechanic II 492565 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Position Summary Performs skilled preventive maintenance, troubleshooting, repair, installation, and service of commercial and institutional HVAC and refrigeration systems with minimal supervision. Works independently on routine and complex mechanical repairs and provides technical assistance to HVAC Mechanic I. The position is responsible for maintaining reliable operation of assigned HVAC equipment and systems and performs work in accordance with established Facilities Services procedures, safety requirements, applicable codes, and manufacturer recommendations. This position is designated as Essential Personnel under College policy and is required to respond during inclement weather, emergency events, and other campus operational needs. Regular Work Schedule Monday\u2013Friday, 8:00 a.m.\u20134:30 p.m., with schedule adjustments, after-hours response, weekends, holidays, and emergency call-back as operationally required. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Performs preventive and corrective maintenance on HVAC equipment and systems. Troubleshoots and repairs commercial HVAC and refrigeration equipment. Repairs and maintains air-handling units, rooftop units, split systems, pumps, motors, exhaust systems, VAV equipment, boilers, chillers, and related equipment. Performs mechanical and electrical troubleshooting associated with HVAC equipment. Replaces motors, drives, belts, bearings, compressors, valves, pumps, controls, and related components. Performs refrigerant recovery, evacuation, charging, and leak detection in accordance with applicable requirements. Uses test instruments and diagnostic equipment to identify equipment problems. Performs equipment startup and operational testing following repairs. Assists with HVAC equipment installation and replacement. Provides technical assistance and guidance to HVAC Mechanic I. Maintains accurate CMMS work orders and equipment records. Maintains assigned tools, equipment, vehicles, and inventory. Responds to emergency HVAC service calls. Follows Lockout/Tagout and other established safety procedures. Assists during campus shutdowns and major repairs. Participates in severe weather and essential personnel activities as required. Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of commercial HVAC and refrigeration systems. Knowledge of refrigeration cycles and refrigerant handling. Knowledge of motors, pumps, compressors, valves, and mechanical components. Knowledge of basic electrical circuits and HVAC controls. Ability to troubleshoot mechanical and electrical problems. Ability to read wiring diagrams, equipment manuals, and basic blueprints. Ability to safely operate hand tools, power tools, and diagnostic equipment. Ability to work independently and prioritize assigned work. Ability to provide technical assistance to less-experienced employees. Ability to maintain accurate maintenance records. Strong customer service and communication skills. Ability to work safely in mechanical rooms, rooftops, confined spaces, and other challenging environments. Minimum Qualifications Education High school diploma or GED required. Completion of an HVAC/R technical program preferred Experience 3\u20135 years of progressively responsible commercial/institutional HVAC experience Licenses EPA Section 608 Universal Certification Preferred Trade school certificate Journeyman certification or equivalent Valid driver\u2019s license with acceptable driving record. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 10a77171 Last Name (required) 00568661 Email (required) 5eeaf639 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) f9f7c9a8 Last Name (required) fad749e8 Email (required) 2cc82015 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/hvac-mechanic-i-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "HVAC Mechanic I", "description": "HVAC Mechanic I - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States HVAC Mechanic I - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode HVAC Mechanic I 492566 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Position Summary Performs entry-level to developing skilled work in the preventive maintenance, inspection, repair, and installation of commercial and institutional HVAC equipment and systems. Works under the direction of the HVAC Supervisor, HVAC Technician III, and HVAC Mechanic II while developing technical proficiency in commercial HVAC maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair. This position is designated as Essential Personnel under College policy and is required to respond during inclement weather, emergency events, and other campus operational needs. Regular Work Schedule Monday\u2013Friday, 8:00 a.m.\u20134:30 p.m., with schedule adjustments, after-hours response, weekends, holidays, and emergency call-back as operationally required. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Performs routine and preventive maintenance on HVAC equipment. Changes filters, belts, pulleys, and other routine maintenance components Lubricates motors, bearings, and other equipment and components as required. Assists with troubleshooting heating, ventilation, refrigeration, and air conditioning systems. Performs routine preventive maintenance on HVAC equipment. Assists with inspection and maintenance of air-handling units, rooftop units, pumps, motors, boilers, chillers, and related equipment. Assists with troubleshooting mechanical and electrical HVAC problems. Assists with routine and emergency HVAC equipment repairs and installations. Assists with refrigerant recovery and other refrigeration work under appropriate supervision. Uses and maintains assigned hand tools, power tools, and basic testing equipment safely. Maintains accurate work order information in the CMMS. Learns campus HVAC systems, equipment, procedures, and safety requirements. Follows Lockout/Tagout and other established safety procedures. Assists with repairs to chillers, boilers, pumps, cooling towers, exhaust systems, and package units. Performs basic electrical and mechanical testing. Provides professional customer service to campus occupants. Participates in emergency response, severe weather operations, and essential personnel activities as required. Performs related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Basic understanding of HVAC principles and equipment. Ability to learn commercial HVAC systems and maintenance procedures. Ability to safely use hand and power tools. Ability to read basic blueprints and equipment manuals and diagrams. Strong customer service and communication skills. Ability to work independently after training. Ability to communicate effectively with coworkers and campus customers. Ability to follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to perform basic mathematical calculations. Ability to learn and use a CMMS. Ability to work safely and effectively in a variety of physical environments. Willingness to develop technical knowledge and skills through training and on-the-job experience. Minimum Qualifications Education High school diploma or GED. Experience One year of HVAC experience or completion of an HVAC technical program. Preferred Commercial HVAC experience in institutional facilities. Completion of an HVAC/R technical program or vocational training. Valid driver\u2019s license with acceptable driving record. Licenses EPA Section 608 Certification (or ability to obtain within six months). Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 73f06874 Last Name (required) 701b7ccd Email (required) c1264fb1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 04542e35 Last Name (required) 8d747d99 Email (required) 17c4cc5b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/hvac-technician-iii-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states-1b96a69e-b85e-4d1d-9773-ae1aba611a91": {"title": "HVAC Technician III", "description": "HVAC Technician III - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States HVAC Technician III - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode HVAC Technician III 492564 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Position Summary Performs highly skilled and advanced technical work involving the diagnosis, maintenance, repair, commissioning, optimization, and operation of complex heating, ventilation, air conditioning, refrigeration, controls, and building automation systems. Serves as the senior technical resource within the HVAC trade and provides technical guidance, mentoring, and field leadership to HVAC Mechanics I and II. In the absence of the HVAC Supervisor, serves as the designated HVAC lead, providing day-to-day technical direction, coordinating emergency response, prioritizing assigned work, and maintaining continuity of HVAC operations within established policies and procedures. The position may be delegated specific supervisory responsibilities by the Facilities Director or HVAC Supervisor. This position is designated as Essential Personnel under College policy and is required to respond during inclement weather, emergency events, and other campus operational needs. Regular Work Schedule(s): Monday\u2013Friday, 8:00 a.m.\u20134:30 p.m., with schedule adjustments, after-hours response, weekends, holidays, and emergency call-back as operationally required. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Performs advanced troubleshooting, repair, maintenance, and installation of complex HVAC systems. Diagnoses electrical, mechanical, refrigeration, pneumatic, and electronic HVAC problems. Troubleshoots Building Automation Systems, controllers, sensors, actuators, variable frequency drives, and related controls. Performs advanced maintenance and repair of chillers, boilers, cooling towers, air-handling units, pumps, VAV systems, rooftop units, refrigeration systems, and related equipment. Performs testing, adjustment, startup, and commissioning of HVAC equipment. Analyzes equipment performance and identifies causes of recurring failures. Provides technical direction and field leadership to HVAC Mechanics I and II. Assists less-experienced employees with troubleshooting, repairs, and proper work methods. Serves as the designated HVAC lead in the absence of the HVAC Supervisor. Coordinates day-to-day technical response to emergency HVAC conditions when the Supervisor is unavailable. Helps prioritize HVAC work based on safety, building operations, equipment criticality, and established departmental priorities. Communicates significant equipment failures, safety concerns, customer issues, and operational conditions to the HVAC Supervisor or Facilities Director. Serves as a technical contact for contractors and vendors when designated. Assists with HVAC capital projects, renovations, equipment replacement, and commissioning. Reviews equipment specifications, control sequences, and installation work for technical accuracy. Supports energy conservation and equipment optimization initiatives. Assists with developing and improving preventive maintenance procedures. Uses CMMS information to document work, equipment condition, repairs, and follow-up requirements. Participates in emergency response, severe weather operations, and essential personnel activities. Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Advanced knowledge of commercial and institutional HVAC systems. Knowledge of refrigeration, chilled water, hot water, steam, hydronic, and air distribution systems. Advanced knowledge of HVAC controls and Building Automation Systems. Knowledge of electrical systems, motors, motor controls, and variable frequency drives. Ability to diagnose complex equipment and system failures. Ability to interpret blueprints, wiring diagrams, equipment manuals, and sequences of operation. Ability to use HVAC diagnostic and testing equipment. Ability to lead technical work and provide instruction to other employees. Ability to make sound technical decisions independently. Ability to communicate technical information effectively. Ability to prioritize work during emergency conditions. Ability to work effectively with contractors, vendors, campus customers, and other Facilities Services personnel. Strong problem-solving and analytical skills. Ability to accurately document work using a CMMS. Minimum Qualifications Education High school diploma or GED required. Technical diploma, certificate, or associate degree in HVAC/R, Mechanical Systems, Building Automation, or a related field preferred. Experience 5 to 7 years of progressively responsible commercial or institutional HVAC experience, including significant experience with complex HVAC systems, controls, and troubleshooting. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education, healthcare, research, or other complex institutional environment. Experience with Building Automation Systems. Experience with central plant systems, chillers, boilers, cooling towers, and hydronic systems. Experience commissioning HVAC equipment and systems. Demonstrated experience providing technical leadership or mentoring to skilled trades employees. Experience with CMMS systems. Experience supporting HVAC capital projects and equipment replacement planning. Valid driver\u2019s license with acceptable driving record. Licenses EPA Section 608 Universal Certification NATE, HVAC Excellence, or comparable industry certification. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) d7fff9c2 Last Name (required) ffd46c4c Email (required) 3564a052 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) a05b7bcc Last Name (required) 85be4373 Email (required) 6cb43992 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/groundskeeper-waste-specialist-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Groundskeeper Waste Specialist", "description": "Groundskeeper Waste Specialist - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Groundskeeper Waste Specialist - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Groundskeeper Waste Specialist 492563 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. General Purpose of Position Position is responsible for the routine care and maintenance of a clean, beautiful and safe campus environment. Works in concert with the grounds team to maintain and enhance the function and aesthetics of the campus grounds. Position is classified as essential personnel under college policy and is subject to college and department policies regarding essential personnel. Performs essential duties as identified by management and incident response team related to inclement or hazardous weather events. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Removes unsightly trash and debris from public areas by regularly inspecting grounds, and collection areas for waste; raking, sweeping and bagging leaves, debris, dirt, and trash from sidewalks, parking lots, and roads Transports waste and recycling to designated collection points on a daily basis Routinely clears of sidewalks, entrances, courtyards, campus roads and parking lots using gas powered blowers Routinely services hallway recycling and exterior recycling stations; monitors, collects, transports and properly disposes of campus recyclables Assists in the routine maintenance of athletic fields and facilities Assists in the repair of brick sidewalks, road signs, parking lots and campus roads surfaces Performs snow and storm related campus clean up, removing debris and snow from sidewalks, parking lots, and building entrances to ensure safe conditions for students, faculty and staff May be required to work during campus closures Performs other related duties as necessary or as assigned by supervisor Skills Needed Must be skilled in the performance of grounds maintenance tasks such as mowing, edging, string-trimming, hedge-trimming, leaf and trash removal Must be able to communicate well and work harmoniously with others Key Interfaces Works closely with Grounds Supervisor and other Grounds Staff Education, Experience, Certifications, etc. High school diploma or GED Grounds and landscape maintenance experience is required Working Conditions & Physical Demands The nature of the working environment may produce moderate levels of stress and involves discomfort and/or risk such as operating gas powered equipment, heavy machinery and dangerous cutting equipment. Workers are subject to environmental discomfort such as frequent exposure to loud noises, and/or extremes of heat or cold The work frequently requires wearing protective gear that may be uncomfortable Must be able to perform strenuous work that involves frequent exertion and/or periods of continuous machine operation Frequent lifting of objects over 50 pounds. Occasional lifting of heavy objects weighing 75 pounds or more is required Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 2d491cec Last Name (required) 3c30abb2 Email (required) 5860774e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) e61eebe6 Last Name (required) d6d3a3b4 Email (required) 7e32c715 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/groundskeeper-tech-and-equipment-specialist-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Groundskeeper Tech and Equipment Specialist", "description": "Groundskeeper Tech and Equipment Specialist - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Groundskeeper Tech and Equipment Specialist - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Groundskeeper Tech and Equipment Specialist 492562 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. This position is for a highly skilled grounds worker/technician specializing in landscaping maintenance, paver repair, and heavy equipment operation. Responsibilities include operating tractors/backhoes, installing/repairing brick pavers, assisting in maintenance of irrigation systems, and ensuring site safety. Requires significant experience with mowing and landscaping machinery and ability to work independently. Required Skills & Qualifications Experience: Minimum of 5 years in grounds maintenance, hardscaping, or related construction field. Technical Knowledge: Proficiency in pavers/masonry repair and site preparation. Machinery Skills: Proven experience operating tractors and heavy machinery. Physical Stamina: Ability to lift up to 75 pounds and work in various weather conditions (extreme heat/cold). Frequent bending, kneeling, lifting, and shoveling. Self-Motivation: Ability to work independently with minimal supervision in a fast-paced environment. Communication: Ability to follow oral and written instructions and report on site conditions Essential Duties and Responsibilities (with Percentage of Time) Turf & Landscaping Management (40%) Operate large zero-turn mowers, edge, and trim to high standards. Maintain plant health via pruning, mulching, and planting. Tractor Operation & Specialized Equipment (20%) Safely operate compact tractors and skid steers with various attachments (mower decks, bush cutters, aerators, augers, loaders) for grading, brush clearing, and loading materials. Perform daily pre-operation inspections, routine maintenance, and cleaning of tractors, mowers, and tools. Paver Repair & Hardscape Maintenance (15%) Repair, level, and relay paver patios, walkways, and retaining walls. Clean, re-sand, and seal paver surfaces. Repair asphalt or concrete cracks and minor drainage issues. Irrigation Maintenance & Repair (10%) Troubleshoot, repair, and adjust irrigation systems, including sprinkler heads, valves, and timers. Winterize irrigation systems and start them up in spring. Seasonal Site Upkeep & Safety (10%) Perform snow removal, salting, and ice management. Conduct fall leaf removal and spring cleanups. Ensure all areas are free of litter and debris. Administrative & Safety (5%) Adhere to all safety regulations. Maintain a clean and safe work environment. Daily reporting and recordkeeping. Position Summary We are seeking a highly skilled and motivated Grounds Maintenance Specialist to join our team. This role goes beyond basic mowing; it requires technical expertise in hardscape/paver repair, advanced tractor operation with attachments, and professional landscape expertise. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 5f5e2e24 Last Name (required) 699ff7f5 Email (required) 3e1eb5ec Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 85c1729f Last Name (required) 5886c09d Email (required) 839e7947 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/director-of-the-lowery-fitness-center-and-campus-recreation-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Director of the Lowery Fitness Center and Campus Recreation", "description": "Director of the Lowery Fitness Center and Campus Recreation - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Director of the Lowery Fitness Center and Campus Recreation - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Director of the Lowery Fitness Center and Campus Recreation 492561 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Position Summary The Director of the Lowery Fitness Center leads the center and creates and develops a robust campus recreation program for Meredith College students. The Director is responsible for the development and operation of the Meredith Intramural Sports Program and the Meredith Outdoor Leadership Program, alongside fitness programming and wellness initiatives for the campus community. Reporting to the Vice President for Student Affairs, the Director manages programs, budgets, facilities, assessment, and risk in collaboration with campus partners. The Lowery Fitness Center also supports teaching and research in Health, Exercise, and Sport Sciences, strength and conditioning for Athletics, and student and employee wellness. The Director coordinates these shared uses so that the center is safe, accessible, and responsive to the needs of its users. Primary Responsibilities Fitness Center Operations and Campus Recreation \u2022 Direct the daily operation of the Lowery Fitness Center, including schedules, facility use, equipment, customer service, and safe operating practices. \u2022 Create and develop a robust campus recreation program with varied, inclusive opportunities for students to participate in fitness, recreation, and active leisure. \u2022 Establish program goals, coordinate space and staffing, promote participation, and assess engagement and effectiveness. \u2022 Recruit, hire, train, schedule, supervise, and evaluate fitness center personnel and student staff; provide recurring onboarding and appropriate emergency response training. \u2022 Manage program and facility budgets, revenue and gift accounts, payroll, purchasing, inventory, equipment, and supplies. Intramural Sports and Outdoor Leadership \u2022 Develop and operate the Meredith Intramural Sports Program, including its schedule, registration, rules, eligibility, officials, staffing, facilities, equipment, promotion, and participation records. \u2022 Develop and operate the Meredith Outdoor Leadership Program through outdoor experiences and leadership development activities. \u2022 Plan outdoor trips and programs; train and supervise leaders; coordinate transportation and equipment; and establish appropriate safety, emergency response, and risk management procedures. Campus Partnerships and Shared Facilities \u2022 Collaborate with Health, Exercise, and Sport Sciences on health literacy courses, laboratory courses, clinical exercise programs, student group fitness, employee wellness classes, and training opportunities in the center. \u2022 Work with the Student Health Center and Human Resources to coordinate and promote fitness and wellness opportunities. \u2022 Collaborate with Athletics to provide assigned strength and conditioning support for student-athletes, coordinate with athletic trainers on injury prevention and return-to-play progressions, and maintain a safe training environment. \u2022 Support the Department of Nutrition, Health, and Human Performance in coordinating additional fitness facilities and laboratories as assigned. Planning Assessment and Risk Management \u2022 Develop annual plans and evaluate the reach, quality, safety, and effectiveness of fitness and recreation programs. \u2022 Track participation and other relevant measures; use student feedback and assessment results to improve programs and report outcomes to the Vice President for Student Affairs. \u2022 Maintain appropriate procedures for supervision, participant safety, medical emergencies, equipment use, travel, and incident response across facilities and programs. Minimum Qualifications \u2022 Master\u2019s degree in kinesiology, exercise science, recreation, sport management, or a related field. \u2022 At least two years of demonstrated experience managing fitness, wellness, recreation, or outdoor programs. \u2022 Knowledge of health, wellness, physical activity, program administration, participant safety, and risk management. \u2022 Current nationally recognized fitness or wellness certification, such as ACE, ACSM, or NSCA, and appropriate first aid and CPR credentials. \u2022 Strong interpersonal, organizational, supervisory, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Experience creating or expanding a campus recreation program, intramural sports program, or outdoor leadership program in higher education. \u2022 Experience teaching physical activity or certification preparation courses and training student staff. \u2022 American Heart Association or American Red Cross instructor certification. \u2022 Relevant strength and conditioning certification through CSCCa, NSCA, or NCSF for any assigned direct work with NCAA student athletes. \u2022 Active involvement in relevant professional organizations. Knowledge Skills and Abilities \u2022 Ability to balance the needs of students, employees, academic programs, and Athletics in a shared facility. \u2022 Ability to plan engaging programs, supervise staff, manage budgets, and assess results. \u2022 Ability to establish sound safety practices and respond effectively to incidents and emergencies. \u2022 Commitment to accessible, inclusive recreation and student development. Required Documents: - Resume/CV - Cover Letter Apply Now! First Name (required) 431d5162 Last Name (required) b8938a48 Email (required) b5686815 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) d611f4db Last Name (required) 62c45582 Email (required) a593b22b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-tennis-coach-part-time-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Tennis Coach, Part-time", "description": "Assistant Tennis Coach, Part-time - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Assistant Tennis Coach, Part-time - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Tennis Coach, Part-time 492560 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Part-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Assistant Women's Tennis Coach supports the Head Coach in the operation of the Meredith College tennis program. This position works closely with the Head Coach to provide a positive, competitive, and student-centered experience for our student-athletes while upholding the mission and values of Meredith College, NCAA Division III, and the USA South Athletic Conference. The assistant coach is expected to be actively involved in coaching, recruiting, game preparation, student-athlete development, and program operations. This position is part-time, less than 20 hours per week and 10 months (position runs from August to May each year). Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Coaching & Player Development - Assist with the planning and implementation of training sessions and practice plans. - Attend and actively coach at team practices, competitions, and team activities as assigned. - Assist with in-game coaching and post-game evaluation. - Provide skill instruction and individual player development. Recruiting - Assist with recruiting efforts for the tennis program. Program Administration - Serve as a driver for team travel when needed. - Help coordinate team events. Compliance & Professional Expectations - Maintain knowledge of and comply with NCAA Division III, USA South Athletic Conference, and Meredith College policies and procedures. - Complete all required NCAA and institutional compliance education. Qualifications: - Bachelor's degree required. - Previous playing or coaching experience in tennis required. - Valid North Carolina driver's license with a clear driving history required. - Ability to travel to all away contests required. - Commitment to the NCAA Division III philosophy and its rules and regulations required. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) d622e823 Last Name (required) 5ea4c7e1 Email (required) bed294a4 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 74dc60bb Last Name (required) b64ca29c Email (required) 9a402471 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/senior-director-of-strategic-giving-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Senior Director of Strategic Giving", "description": "Senior Director of Strategic Giving - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Senior Director of Strategic Giving - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Senior Director of Strategic Giving 492558 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Senior Director is a senior frontline fundraiser responsible for securing significant philanthropic support for Meredith College and leading the performance of the College's major gift fundraising program. Reporting to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, the Senior Director manages a portfolio of major and principal gift prospects and donors while supervising and coaching frontline development officers who advance relationships and secure significant philanthropic commitments. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The Senior Director provides oversight and leads the frontline fundraising team. The position establishes clear expectations for portfolio performance, provides regular coaching and prospect strategy guidance, participates in joint donor visits and solicitations, and holds gift officers accountable for meaningful donor engagement, solicitations, pipeline development, and fundraising results. Working closely with the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, the Senior Director helps translate institutional and campaign priorities into compelling philanthropic opportunities and executes strategies for high-capacity prospects. While the position carries significant responsibility for the performance of the major gifts program, the Senior Director is expected to remain actively engaged in direct fundraising and to model effective relationship-based fundraising for the development team. Major and Principal Gift Fundraising - 50% - Manage an active portfolio of approximately 50-75 major and principal gift prospects and donors, with responsibility for qualification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship. - Develop and execute individualized strategies to move prospects toward significant philanthropic commitments. - Maintain a robust schedule of substantive donor visits and demonstrate consistent progress toward established fundraising and portfolio goals. - Personally solicit and close major, principal, planned, and campaign gifts in support of College priorities. - Build long-term relationships with alumnae, parents, friends, and other constituents with significant philanthropic capacity. - Identify opportunities to increase donors' philanthropic engagement over time, including multi-year, blended, and planned gift opportunities. - Partner with the Vice President, President, trustees, faculty, and other College leaders when their involvement can advance significant donor relationships and solicitations. - Model disciplined, donor-centered portfolio management and effective major gift fundraising practices for the development team. Frontline Fundraising Leadership and Supervision - 25% - Supervise, coach, and develop frontline major gift officers and other assigned development staff. - Establish individual fundraising, solicitation, visit, and portfolio goals aligned with overall Institutional Advancement priorities, in consultation with the Vice President. - Conduct regular one-on-one meetings and portfolio strategy sessions focused on prospect movement, pipeline development, solicitations, and fundraising results. - Hold gift officers accountable for effective portfolio management, meaningful donor engagement, timely solicitations, and progress toward established goals. - Provide ongoing coaching and professional development to strengthen fundraising skills and individual performance. - Partner with gift officers on complex and high-value prospects while maintaining clarity regarding primary relationship management and portfolio ownership. - Participate in joint donor visits and solicitations when senior-level involvement will strengthen a relationship or help advance a significant gift. - Foster a collaborative, accountable, and donor-centered fundraising culture. - Partner with Prospect Development to evaluate portfolio composition, identify new prospects, monitor pipeline health, and ensure appropriate deployment of frontline fundraising resources. - Participate in recruitment, onboarding, and development of frontline fundraising staff as needed. Campaign and Principal Gift Strategy - 20% - Partner with the Vice President for Institutional Advancement to execute fundraising strategies for the College's comprehensive campaign and other major institutional priorities. - Develop and implement strategies for high-capacity prospects connected to campaign priorities. - Help translate institutional priorities into compelling and appropriately scaled philanthropic opportunities. - Collaborate on major and principal gift proposals, naming opportunities, gift concepts, and donor-facing materials. - Assist the Vice President in preparing the President and other senior leaders for significant donor meetings and solicitations. - Work with trustees and campaign volunteers on specific prospect introductions, cultivation strategies, and solicitations. - Partner closely with Senior Director of Planned Giving and other development colleagues to identify and structure blended and complex gift opportunities. - Build the pipeline of future major and principal gift donors through disciplined qualification, cultivation, and engagement strategies. Administration and Institutional Engagement - 5% - Maintain accurate and timely documentation of donor interactions, strategies, proposals, and commitments in the College's advancement database. - Monitor individual and team fundraising performance and provide the Vice President with regular assessments of progress, opportunities, and challenges. - Represent Meredith College at donor meetings, alumnae events, campaign activities, and other College functions. - Build productive relationships with academic and administrative leaders to understand institutional priorities and connect those priorities with donor interests. - Maintain the highest standards of professionalism, confidentiality, ethical fundraising, and donor stewardship. Qualifications: Education and Experience: - Bachelor's degree required; advanced degree or CAP@/CFRE preferred. - At least 7 years of progressive fundraising or related experience. Familiarity with higher education and single gender education is preferred. - Demonstrated success closing six- and seven-figure planned or blended gifts. - Knowledge of charitable tax law, estate planning, trusts, retirement assets, and non-cash gifts. - Proven supervisory and coaching experience. - Valid NC drivers license and a clear driving history is required. Skills Needed: - Exceptional communication and relationship-building skills. - Excellent interpersonal skills. - Ability to prioritize and handle multiple projects. - Leadership and management skills with the ability to establish objectives and set performance standards. - Strong oral and written communication skills. - Understanding of donor recognition and stewardship. - Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as a collaborative member of a team. - Willingness to handle a heavy workload and irregular hours - including some weekends and holidays. - Knowledge of Crescendo Gift Legacy, CresPrint, and CresPro platforms. - Experience with Blackbaud Raiser's Edge NXT or similar CRM platform preferred. Working Conditions & Physical Demands: - General office setting with moderate noise level. - May have to travel long distances occasionally. - May have to work nights and weekends. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 929100c9 Last Name (required) 96404106 Email (required) d1d81033 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 7d95be4e Last Name (required) 7f65276a Email (required) 2d67954d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/associate-director-of-student-success-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Associate Director of Student Success", "description": "Associate Director of Student Success - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Associate Director of Student Success - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Associate Director of Student Success 492556 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Associate Director of Student Success provides leadership and direct student support within the Student Success Center, advancing a student-centered approach to academic advising, success coaching, retention, persistence, and timely degree completion. The position provides comprehensive academic advising and success coaching while developing personalized support strategies that respond to students\u2019 individual goals, needs, strengths, and barriers to success. The Associate Director leads proactive retention and academic recovery efforts, including early outreach, intervention, success planning, and programs designed to promote student engagement and academic progress. The position serves as a senior resource to Student Success Advisors and collaborates with faculty mentors, academic departments, and campus partners to address complex student needs and strengthen coordinated pathways to student success. As a member of the Student Success Center leadership team, the Associate Director contributes to strategic planning, student success initiatives, assessment, and continuous improvement while helping advance an effective, student-centered model of advising, coaching, and retention support. The Associate Director reports directly to the Director of Student Success and contributes to the strategic direction, assessment, and continuous improvement of the Student Success Center. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Student Success, Advising & Coaching - Provide comprehensive academic advising and success coaching to an assigned caseload of students from entry through graduation. - Develop personalized support strategies that address individual student goals, needs, strengths, and barriers to academic success. - Support students with academic planning, degree progression, course selection, registration, goal setting, major exploration, and graduation planning. - Promote student development, self-advocacy, academic ownership, and informed decision-making. Retention, Outreach & Academic Recovery - Develop and implement proactive strategies that promote student engagement, academic progress, persistence, and degree completion. - Conduct outreach and coordinate timely interventions for students experiencing academic difficulty, disengagement, or other barriers to success. - Develop personalized success plans, facilitate success strategy meetings, and support students participating in academic recovery initiatives. - Monitor student progress and adjust support strategies as appropriate. Student Success Programs & Initiatives - Develop, coordinate, and facilitate student success workshops, programs, and educational initiatives that address identified student needs. - Lead designated initiatives related to academic success, student engagement, transition, retention, persistence, and student development. - Collaborate with campus departments and subject-matter experts to develop and deliver effective student success programming. Collaboration & Student Advocacy - Serve as a senior resource and collaborative partner to Student Success Advisors regarding complex student situations, retention strategies, and academic recovery. - Collaborate with faculty mentors, academic departments, and campus partners to support student progress and persistence. - Establish effective communication and referral pathways and advocate for students navigating academic and institutional processes. Assessment, Technology & Continuous Improvement - Use student success, advising, retention, and engagement data to identify student needs and inform interventions, programs, and advising practices. - Contribute to assessment, reporting, and continuous improvement efforts in collaboration with the Director and Student Success Operations, Systems & Assessment Coordinator. - Utilize advising, degree audit, early alert, student information, and student success technologies while maintaining accurate and timely student documentation. Strategic Leadership & Professional Responsibilities - Serve as a member of the Student Success Center leadership team and contribute to the Center's strategic direction, priorities, policies, and service standards. - Lead designated projects and initiatives and collaborate with the Director and Associate Director of Student Success & Learning Center on center-wide efforts. - Maintain current knowledge of academic advising, student development, retention, and student success practices. - Participate in professional development and institutional initiatives and perform other duties as assigned in support of the mission of the Student Success Center. Minimum Required Qualifications: - Master\u2019s degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, academic advising, education, or a related field. - Minimum of 3 years of progressive experience in higher education, with experience in academic advising, student success, retention, student development, or a related area. - Strong interpersonal, communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills. - Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, academic departments, and campus partners. - Commitment to proactive, student-centered approaches that support student persistence, academic achievement, and degree completion. Preferred Qualifications: - 5 years of progressive experience in higher education with experience in academic advising, student success, retention, or related areas. - Experience with EAB Navigate 360 or a comparable student success, advising, or early-alert platform. - Experience developing and implementing personalized success plans, academic recovery initiatives, early interventions, or retention strategies. - Experience leading student success workshops, programs, or campus-wide initiatives. - Experience working with degree audit, student information, advising, early-alert, and other student success technologies. - Experience using assessment and student success data to evaluate programs and improve services. - Experience supporting students from diverse backgrounds and with varying academic, personal, and institutional needs. - Knowledge of current practices and trends in academic advising, student development, retention, and college student success. Review of applications will begin on Monday, October 5, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 3e6703b0 Last Name (required) 68a753f8 Email (required) d8628a2e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) ea2ecebf Last Name (required) 75504639 Email (required) d10545d5 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/associate-director-of-student-success-and-learning-center-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Associate Director of Student Success and Learning Center", "description": "Associate Director of Student Success and Learning Center - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Associate Director of Student Success and Learning Center - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Associate Director of Student Success and Learning Center 492555 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Associate Director of Student Success & Learning Center provides leadership for the Meredith College Learning Center while supporting the broader mission of the Student Success Center. The position oversees tutoring and academic learning support programs, including tutor recruitment, training, scheduling, development, and evaluation. The Associate Director also provides comprehensive academic advising and success coaching to an assigned caseload of students across class years and academic programs. The position develops personalized academic support strategies, implements proactive interventions for students experiencing academic challenges, and collaborates with faculty mentors, academic departments, Student Success Advisors, Disability Services, and other campus partners. The Associate Director also contributes to student success programming, retention initiatives, assessment, and continuous improvement efforts within the Student Success Center. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Academic Support & Student Success - Provide comprehensive academic advising and success coaching to an assigned caseload of students from entry to graduation. - Support students with academic planning, degree progression, course selection, registration, goal setting, and graduation planning. - Develop personalized support strategies addressing students' academic goals, strengths, needs, and barriers to success. - Provide academic support related to study strategies, time management, organization, test preparation, and other learning skills. - Develop proactive outreach and interventions for students experiencing academic difficulty or who may benefit from additional support. - Facilitate success strategy meetings, contribute to individualized success plans, and support academic recovery efforts. - Connect students with tutoring, Learning Center resources, and appropriate campus services. Learning Center Leadership & Management - Provide leadership and oversight of the Meredith College Learning Center and its tutoring and academic learning support programs. - Recruit, hire, train, schedule, mentor, and evaluate peer tutors in collaboration with academic departments and campus partners. - Develop and maintain effective tutor training, professional development, and evaluation processes, including coordination of IDS 155: Tutor Training. - Manage tutor schedules, timesheets, and working hours and oversee day-to-day Learning Center operations. - Manage the Learning Center budget in collaboration with the Director of Student Success. - Monitor Learning Center utilization, staffing, and student needs to support effective delivery of services. - Maintain and advance CRLA certification and ensure tutoring practices align with established professional standards. Collaboration & Coordination - Collaborate with faculty mentors, Student Success Advisors, academic departments, Disability Services, and other campus partners to coordinate academic support. - Serve as a resource to faculty and staff regarding tutoring, academic learning support, student success strategies, and appropriate referrals. - Establish effective referral and communication pathways between the Learning Center and other student support services. - Contribute to Student Success Center retention initiatives, workshops, and other programs that promote academic achievement and persistence. Assessment, Technology & Continuous Improvement - Collect and analyze data related to tutoring participation, student engagement, academic support utilization, and student outcomes. - Use assessment findings to evaluate Learning Center services, identify student needs, and inform program improvements. - Utilize advising, degree audit, early alert, student information, and student success technologies. - Maintain accurate and timely documentation of student interactions, tutoring services, and program activities. Strategic Leadership & Professional Responsibilities - Contribute to the strategic direction, policies, and service standards of the Student Success Center. - Maintain current knowledge of academic advising, tutoring, learning strategies, student development, retention, and student success practices. - Participate in professional development, institutional initiatives, and other duties that support the mission of the Student Success Center. Minimum Required Qualifications: - Master's degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, education, psychology, social work, sociology, or a related field. - Minimum of 3 years of progressive experience in higher education, academic advising, student success, learning support, tutoring, or a related area. - Strong communication, organization, interpersonal, problem-solving, and collaboration skills. - Proficiency with Microsoft Office and Google Workspace. Preferred Qualifications: - 5 or more years of progressive experience in higher education, academic advising, student success, learning support, tutoring, or a related area. - Experience with college tutoring, curriculum development, and/or supervising student/peer tutors - Experience with EAB Navigate/Navigate 360 - Experience recruiting, training, supervising, mentoring, or evaluating student employees, peer tutors, or similar student staff. - Experience leading a college or university learning center, tutoring program, or academic support program. - Experience using student success and assessment data to evaluate programs and improve services. Review of applications will begin on Monday, October 5, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 0cb9715f Last Name (required) 5bf18402 Email (required) 7597cea9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) c12929e8 Last Name (required) 3b5e9a23 Email (required) dc7c467a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/security-officer-3rd-shift-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Security Officer, 3rd Shift", "description": "Security Officer, 3rd Shift - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Security Officer, 3rd Shift - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Security Officer, 3rd Shift 492554 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Provides safety, security, customer service, and emergency response services to students, faculty, staff, visitors, and campus guests through the effective use of departmental resources and proactive patrol activities. Supports the mission of the Campus Police & Security Department by protecting life and property, maintaining a safe campus environment, enforcing College policies, responding to calls for service, and assisting with emergency response operations. Position is classified as essential personnel under College policy and is subject to College and department policies regarding essential personnel. Performs essential duties related to security work as identified by management during inclement weather, emergency situations, campus closures, or as operational needs dictate. Third Shift hours: 11pm \u2013 7am Essential Duties & Responsibilities: - Provides exceptional customer service and assistance while maintaining a safe and secure campus environment. - Determines and takes appropriate action to resolve incidents, safety concerns, and requests for service in accordance with College policies and departmental procedures. May be required to utilize minimum levels of force consistent with training and departmental policy. - Patrols campus by vehicle and foot, including academic buildings, residence halls, parking lots, athletic facilities, and other College property to identify safety and security concerns. - Controls access to campus facilities and the Greenway during designated hours and assists with access control functions, including unlocking and securing facilities in accordance with College procedures. - Responds to and investigates security, fire, panic, and intrusion alarm activations and takes appropriate action. - Conducts routine safety and security inspections of campus facilities, including checking doors, windows, lighting, and other security-related infrastructure. - Enforces parking regulations, including issuing citations, coordinating towing and vehicle immobilization, and providing traffic control during special events and campus activities. - Provides vehicle assistance services, including jump starts, vehicle unlocks, and other approved assistance to students, faculty, and staff. - Assists with emergency response activities, evacuations, severe weather operations, campus emergencies, and incident management procedures. - Provides basic assistance during medical emergencies, including First Aid, CPR, and AED response, until relieved by emergency medical personnel. - Assists with special events, athletic events, commencement activities, move-in/move-out operations, and other campus functions. - Documents incidents, suspicious activity, safety concerns, and operational issues through reports, logs, and other departmental documentation. - Reports safety hazards, maintenance concerns, security vulnerabilities, and other operational issues to appropriate personnel. - Assists with turning campus lighting on and off for special events, athletic activities, and other approved functions. - Maintains assigned equipment, vehicles, uniforms, and other departmental resources in a safe and operational condition. - Performs duties related to inclement weather operations, emergency response, campus closures, and other essential personnel responsibilities as assigned. - Performs other related duties as assigned. Skills Needed: - Ability to exercise sound judgment and discretion when handling difficult situations and interacting with diverse populations. - Ability to observe and retain names, faces, details of occurrences, and other information necessary for report writing and investigations. - Ability to maintain accurate records, prepare reports, and complete required documentation. - Ability to understand and operate security systems, emergency alarm systems, radios, and other departmental equipment. - Ability to interpret, apply, and explain College policies, procedures, and departmental guidelines. - Ability to communicate effectively and professionally, both verbally and in writing. - Ability to remain calm and respond appropriately during emergencies, critical incidents, and stressful situations. - Ability to provide excellent customer service while maintaining safety and security responsibilities. - Ability to observe legal and defensive driving practices and safely operate departmental vehicles. Key interfaces: - Students, faculty, staff, visitors, parents, contractors, vendors, and campus guests. - Security Supervisors, Police Officers, and other departmental personnel. - Residence Life, Student Affairs, Facilities Services, Athletics, Conference & Event Services, and other campus departments. - Raleigh Police Department, fire departments, EMS providers, and other emergency response agencies as needed. - Individuals experiencing emergencies, conflicts, behavioral concerns, or other situations requiring security assistance. Education & Experience: - High School Diploma or equivalent required. - Valid North Carolina Driver License with an acceptable driving record. - Previous experience in security, customer service, public safety, law enforcement, military service, emergency response, or related fields preferred. - CPR, First Aid, and AED Certification preferred or ability to obtain within a designated period following employment. Working conditions & physical demands: - Must be able to work assigned shifts, including days, evenings, nights, weekends, holidays, special events, and emergency call-back situations. - Work is performed in office, vehicle, and outdoor environments and may involve exposure to varying weather conditions. - May be required to remain on duty during emergencies, inclement weather events, or campus closures when relief personnel are unavailable. - Requires the ability to walk extended distances, stand for prolonged periods, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and respond to emergencies throughout campus. - Requires the ability to safely operate departmental vehicles and security equipment. - Ability to assist individuals experiencing medical emergencies, mobility challenges, or other safety-related concerns. - May occasionally lift, carry, move, or position equipment, supplies, or materials weighing up to 50 pounds. - Requires the ability to communicate effectively and perform the essential functions of the position in both routine and emergency situations. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 5e96e0a8 Last Name (required) 3362794f Email (required) 30c5535a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) d3e9b6fc Last Name (required) 4f32de42 Email (required) 05fd47b3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/police-officer-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Police Officer", "description": "Police Officer - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Police Officer - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Police Officer 492519 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Provides comprehensive law enforcement, safety, and security services to students, faculty, staff, and visitors through the efficient use of departmental resources. Enforces applicable federal laws, North Carolina General Statutes, and Meredith College policies. This position is classified as essential personnel under College policy and is subject to requirements regarding essential personnel. Performs essential police duties during inclement weather, emergency situations, or as campus needs dictate. This role also supports a developing campus police department by contributing to the continuous improvement of operations, procedures, and service delivery, while helping to foster a culture of professionalism, accountability, and community engagement. Duties: - Responds to all calls for service and requests for assistance from Meredith College students, faculty, staff, and visitors - Exercises independent judgment to determine appropriate actions to resolve incidents, including detention, search, arrest, issuance of citations, and criminal charge filing in accordance with North Carolina law - Applies only the minimum level of force necessary, consistent with training, law, and departmental policy - Patrols campus by vehicle and on foot; operates a law enforcement patrol vehicle during day and night shifts - Controls access to campus facilities and designated areas, including the Greenway, during established hours - Responds to calls, fire alarms, and intrusion alarms, including suspicious persons, and takes appropriate enforcement or protective action - Conducts preliminary and follow-up investigations by interviewing victims, witnesses, suspects, and confidential informants; collects, preserves, and documents physical and digital evidence - Prepares detailed written reports, case files, and documentation in accordance with departmental policy and legal standards - Provides testimony in criminal, traffic, and judicial proceedings as required - Provides traffic, parking, and crowd control for campus events and special functions - Conducts safety and security inspections of campus facilities, including checking doors, windows, and lighting - Renders emergency and non-emergency medical assistance, including First Aid, CPR, and AED use, until relieved by medical professionals - Participates in community-oriented policing, crime prevention initiatives, campus outreach, and educational programming - Builds positive relationships with students, faculty, and staff through visibility, engagement, and service - May perform administrative duties such as campus bank deposits or other assignments as directed - Performs duties related to emergency response, disaster operations, and inclement weather safety responsibilities - Participates in the development and refinement of departmental practices, procedures, and service delivery models - Provides feedback to supervisors to support the growth and continuous improvement of a developing department Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: - Knowledge of federal laws, North Carolina General Statutes, and College policies applicable to sworn law enforcement officers - Ability to analyze complex situations, exercise sound judgment, and use discretion when dealing with difficult or hostile individuals - Ability to observe and recall names, faces, and details; maintain accurate notes and reports - Skill in operating law enforcement equipment, including radios, vehicles, and defensive tools - Ability to communicate clearly and professionally with diverse populations - Ability to understand and work within the scope of authority while applying policies and procedures consistently - Ability to adapt to evolving policies, procedures, and operational needs in a developing department - Commitment to maintaining the highest standards of integrity, professionalism, and ethical conduct Education & Experience: - High School Diploma or equivalent required - Current North Carolina Driver License with a clear driving history - Current certification as a sworn Law Enforcement Officer by the State of North Carolina (BLET) Training & Certification Requirements: - Successful completion of required in-service training and annual firearms qualification - Certification or ability to obtain certification in ASP baton, chemical agents, First Aid, CPR, and AED - Compliance with North Carolina Criminal Justice Education and Training Standards Commission requirements - Successful completion of a basic physical fitness assessment prior to appointment and/or during probationary period, consistent with departmental standards Working conditions & physical demands: - Ability to work modified 3rd shift (6 p.m. \u2013 2 a.m.), rotating shifts, including nights, weekends, holidays, and emergency call-back - Duties performed in office, vehicle, and outdoor environments; subject to varying weather conditions - May be required to remain on duty during inclement weather or emergencies when relief is unavailable - Medium work: ability to walk extended distances, stand for long periods, climb stairs, run as necessary, and lift up to 50 pounds - Ability to navigate physical obstacles and assist individuals experiencing medical or safety emergencies - Vision correctable to meet North Carolina law enforcement standards, including color vision requirements Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 5f1b3dd7 Last Name (required) 8c019b19 Email (required) 8690d4e1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 82af5512 Last Name (required) 7a609cbf Email (required) 52f1d4e2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/office-and-billing-manager-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Office and Billing Manager (Admin II)", "description": "Office and Billing Manager (Admin II) - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Office and Billing Manager (Admin II) - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Office and Billing Manager (Admin II) 492551 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Responsible for the upkeep of fiscal matters including insurance billing, student records and supply budget. Serve as HIPAA Privacy and Security Officer for MAP. Assist with the maintenance of MAP policies and procedures. Provide support to the program director and associate director. Duties: - Work directly with MAP contracted billing agencies including the MC Accounting Office and any outside contractors for monthly MAP client billing. - Keep track of all client treatment plan authorizations and ensure concurrent authorizations are submitted accurately and by due date. - Ensure all new staff and students have completed necessary paperwork and agreements before beginning work and are added to necessary portals (i.e. data collection, etc). - Onboard new BCBA staff by working to get them credentialed with insurance providers. - Complete session note checks for all clients in data collection software to ensure that session notes and times match before billing for these services. - Run monthly Dropbox and Motivity security checks. - Actively seek out and remain up to date on monthly changes to insurance company policies, billing and authorizations. - Update families promptly with regard to insurance benefits and how those benefits are applied to billing. - Collect and document all coinsurance, copayments, and tuition payments, as well as scholarship awards, and apply to each client\u2019s account. - Provide monthly bills to families and follow up to ensure payments are made and recorded. - Serve as HIPAA Privacy and Security Officer for MAP a. Responsibilities as the HIPAA Security Officer for MAP, with the following job duties: i. Overseeing the MAP HIPAA Security Compliance Program & policies and procedures ii. Providing periodic security reminders for MAP staff iii. Being a point of contact for HIPAA Security questions or complaints iv. Liaison with the Meredith IT Department related to compliance of HIPAA Security technical safeguards operated by IT v. Ensuring periodic evaluations of the HIPAA Security compliance program vi. Ensuring periodic PHI risk analysis and a corresponding risk management program b. Responsibilities as the HIPAA Privacy Officer for MAP, with the following job duties: i. Overseeing the MAP HIPAA Privacy Compliance Program & policies and procedures ii. Acting as a point of contact for HIPAA Privacy questions or complaints iii. Ensuring HIPAA Privacy compliance for MAP forms related to uses and disclosures of protected health information iv. Investigating parent or client HIPAA privacy complaints v. Reporting any PHI breaches as required by the HIPAA breach notification requirements - Continuously update training to ensure knowledge of HIPAA regulations. - Prioritize, maintain, and oversee MAP paperwork and policies for client confidentiality and HIPAA regulations to ensure that MAP remains in compliance. - Routinely update and maintain/document MAP paperwork and policies to support renewal of MAP\u2019s DHHS license and ensure compliance with all DHHS regulations. - Work with Program Director and Associate Director in overseeing and maintaining Facility and Supply budgets. - Assist Program Director and Associate Director in tracking and acknowledging gifts received by the program. - Complete monthly credit card billing statements accurately and in a timely manner. - Run occasional errands, maintain supplies, and otherwise maintain a functional and efficient office. - Ensure proper maintenance of all client records. - Responsible for submitting and following up on facility work order requests - Submit for renewal of DHHS license each year - Opens and/or Closes facility as scheduled. - Ensure proper documentation of student and client incident reports - Work with the Program Director and Associate Director to prioritize other duties as assigned. Qualifications: EITHER - High school diploma and a minimum of three years experience in a similar position. Experience in educational setting is preferred. OR - Bachelor\u2019s degree and a minimum of 1 year of experience Requirements: - Demonstrated competency in the field of online medical/mental/behavioral health insurance billing and coding. - At least one year of billing experience using electronic systems for an organization. - Demonstrated competency in all basic user software systems such as Word, Excel, Google Docs and Publisher - Demonstrated knowledge of HIPAA rules and regulations - Have at least one year experience working with an agency conducting in-network insurance billing - Have no substantiated finding of abuse or neglect listed on the North Carolina Health Care Personnel Registry. Preferred Qualifications: - Experience working with in-network billing for a behavioral healthcare provider in the state of North Carolina. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 440e8c27 Last Name (required) 3777e6c1 Email (required) e5740286 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 85d4eb9c Last Name (required) 59856aa0 Email (required) a4797ec1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/police-officer-part-time-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Police Officer, Part-time", "description": "Police Officer, Part-time - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Police Officer, Part-time - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Police Officer, Part-time 492552 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Part-time Closing at: Oct 27 2026 - 11:55pm EDT Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Provides comprehensive law enforcement, safety, and security services on a part-time basis to students, faculty, staff, and visitors through the efficient use of departmental resources. Enforces applicable federal laws, North Carolina General Statutes, and Meredith College policies. This position is classified as essential personnel under College policy and is subject to requirements regarding essential personnel. Performs essential police duties during inclement weather, emergency situations, or as campus needs dictate. This role also supports a developing campus police department by contributing to the continuous improvement of operations, procedures, and service delivery, while helping to foster a culture of professionalism, accountability, and community engagement. This position is for 2nd, 3rd and weekend shifts. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: - Responds to all calls for service and requests for assistance from Meredith College students, faculty, staff, and visitors - Exercises independent judgment to determine appropriate actions to resolve incidents, including detention, search, arrest, issuance of citations, and criminal charge filing in accordance with North Carolina law - Applies only the minimum level of force necessary, consistent with training, law, and departmental policy - Patrols campus by vehicle and on foot; operates a law enforcement patrol vehicle during day and night shifts - Controls access to campus facilities and designated areas, including the Greenway, during established hours - Responds to calls, fire alarms, and intrusion alarms, including suspicious persons, and takes appropriate enforcement or protective action - Conducts preliminary and follow-up investigations by interviewing victims, witnesses, suspects, and confidential informants; collects, preserves, and documents physical and digital evidence - Prepares detailed written reports, case files, and documentation in accordance with departmental policy and legal standards - Provides testimony in criminal, traffic, and judicial proceedings as required - Provides traffic, parking, and crowd control for campus events and special functions - Conducts safety and security inspections of campus facilities, including checking doors, windows, and lighting - Renders emergency and non-emergency medical assistance, including First Aid, CPR, and AED use, until relieved by medical professionals - Participates in community-oriented policing, crime prevention initiatives, campus outreach, and educational programming - Builds positive relationships with students, faculty, and staff through visibility, engagement, and service - May perform administrative duties such as campus bank deposits or other assignments as directed - Performs duties related to emergency response, disaster operations, and inclement weather safety responsibilities - Participates in the development and refinement of departmental practices, procedures, and service delivery models - Provides feedback to supervisors to support the growth and continuous improvement of a developing department Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: - Knowledge of federal laws, North Carolina General Statutes, and College policies applicable to sworn law enforcement officers - Ability to analyze complex situations, exercise sound judgment, and use discretion when dealing with difficult or hostile individuals - Ability to observe and recall names, faces, and details; maintain accurate notes and reports - Skill in operating law enforcement equipment, including radios, vehicles, and defensive tools - Ability to communicate clearly and professionally with diverse populations - Ability to understand and work within the scope of authority while applying policies and procedures consistently - Ability to adapt to evolving policies, procedures, and operational needs in a developing department - Commitment to maintaining the highest standards of integrity, professionalism, and ethical conduct Education & Experience: - High School Diploma or equivalent required - Current North Carolina Driver License with a clear driving history - Current certification as a sworn Law Enforcement Officer by the State of North Carolina (BLET) Training & Certification Requirements: - Successful completion of required annual in-service training and annual firearms qualification - Compliance with North Carolina Criminal Justice Education and Training Standards Commission requirements - Certification in or ability to obtain certification in First Aid, CPR, AED, ASP Baton, chemical agents, and other department-approved law enforcement tools and techniques - Successful completion of a basic physical fitness assessment prior to appointment and/or during probationary period, consistent with departmental standards Working conditions & physical demands: - Ability to work assigned part-time shifts, including nights, weekends, holidays, and emergency call-back - Duties performed in office, vehicle, and outdoor environments; subject to varying weather conditions - May be required to remain on duty during inclement weather or emergencies when relief is unavailable - Medium work: ability to walk extended distances, stand for long periods, climb stairs, run as necessary, and lift up to 50 pounds - Ability to navigate physical obstacles and assist individuals experiencing medical or safety emergencies - Vision correctable to meet North Carolina law enforcement standards, including color vision requirements Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) e294e3bd Last Name (required) 7b279048 Email (required) 6c2dd957 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 5cbaee16 Last Name (required) c62d8068 Email (required) ae323bb3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-housekeeping-shift-supervisor-2nd-shift-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states-923a47b8-8768-4a82-b75e-f96704c8614d": {"title": "Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor - 2nd Shift", "description": "Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor - 2nd Shift - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor - 2nd Shift - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor - 2nd Shift 492550 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor serves as the lead worker for an assigned shift and assists the Housekeeping Shift Supervisor with the daily coordination of housekeeping operations. This position provides work direction, training, quality inspections, and operational support while also performing custodial duties. The Assistant Shift Supervisor helps ensure assigned facilities are maintained in a clean, safe, sanitary, and welcoming condition and supports the supervisor in maintaining productivity, customer service, safety, and quality standards. This position is designated as Essential Personnel under College policy and is required to respond during inclement weather, emergency events, and other campus operational needs. Regular Work Schedule: 2nd Shift: Monday through Friday, 2:00 p.m.- 10:30pm. Weekend and overtime work may be required based on operational needs. Duties: Daily Operations - Assist with coordinating daily work assignments and building coverage. - Assign and prioritize routine and special project work. - Monitor completion of assigned work and adjust assignments as operational needs change. - Perform quality inspections of completed work. - Assist with event support and project scheduling. - Ensure custodial supplies and equipment are available and properly maintained. Leadership - Provide day-to-day direction and guidance to housekeeping staff. - Train new employees in cleaning procedures, equipment operation, and safety practices. - Demonstrate proper custodial methods and departmental standards. - Assist with onboarding new employees. - Promote teamwork and positive employee relations. - Communicate departmental expectations and operational updates. Custodial Support - Perform all duties of a Housekeeper II as operational needs require. - Assist with specialized floor care and project work. - Respond to customer requests and building concerns. Safety & Compliance - Monitor compliance with departmental procedures and safety regulations. - Report equipment issues and facility deficiencies. - Assist with incident documentation. - Support emergency response and inclement weather operations. Administrative Support - Assist the Shift Supervisor with attendance monitoring, supply inventories, work orders, and operational documentation. - Provide input regarding employee performance and training needs. - Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: - Thorough knowledge of custodial methods and cleaning standards. - Ability to lead and motivate employees. - Ability to organize work assignments and prioritize competing demands. - Ability to inspect work for quality. - Strong interpersonal and customer service skills. - Ability to resolve routine workplace issues. - Ability to follow verbal and written instructions. - Ability to communicate effectively and professionally both verbally and in writing. - Proficiency with custodial equipment and cleaning chemicals. Education & Experience: - Minimum of 1 year of progressively responsible custodial experience. - Supervisory or lead experience preferred. - Demonstrated leadership and organizational skills. - Experience in training or leading employees preferred. Working conditions & physical demands: - Works in moderate noise all around campus, indoor and outdoor. - Frequent standing, walking, bending, use of repetitive motions and operating cleaning equipment. - Often lifts 10-50 lbs objects. - May be required to work during periods of inclement weather. - May be required to work weekends. Apply Now! First Name (required) 24ef2627 Last Name (required) eaef7b5d Email (required) 6cc87229 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) b9bc0b87 Last Name (required) 8b37527b Email (required) 65cc58b6 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-to-the-vice-president-for-marketing-and-communications-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Assistant to the Vice President for Marketing and Communications", "description": "Assistant to the Vice President for Marketing and Communications - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Assistant to the Vice President for Marketing and Communications - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Assistant to the Vice President for Marketing and Communications 492548 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The position serves as an executive partner to the Vice President of Marketing and Communications and performs high level administrative and project coordination tasks for a comprehensive, high volume Marketing and Communications Division. The position works with a high degree of confidentiality and requires discretion in handling sensitive conversations and documents, as well as maintaining strict confidentiality when supporting projects that involve executive leadership, trustees, prospective donors, high profile partners, or matters affecting the College\u2019s brand and reputation. Duties: - Manages confidential information related to institutional strategy, personnel, budgets, contracts, external relations on behalf of the VPMC. - Actively manages the calendar and serves as a gatekeeper helping to ensure strategic focus for the VPMC. - Initiates, composes, reviews, and edits correspondence, presentations proposals, and announcements for the Vice President for Marketing and Communications. - Develops and maintains divisional databases, spreadsheets, project trackers, status reports, and other information-management tools to support executive priorities, monitor progress, and ensure timely follow-through. - Supports the Vice President for Marketing and Communications in planning, coordinating, and advancing strategic projects and initiatives, including tracking progress, coordinating stakeholders, and ensuring timely follow-through. - Supports divisional financial administration by maintaining budget records, monitoring designated budget lines, processing expense reports, and assisting with accounts payable and receivable. - Provides administrative and coordination support for divisional digital marketing operations, including website compliance and quality assurance, calendar entries, online marketing profiles, implementing intranet pages, and documentation and follow-up for web strategy meetings. - Provides administrative support for divisional revenue-generating activities, including scheduling, room reservations, facility tours, client documentation, event agreements, insurance, billing, and client tracking. - Occasionally supports the Campus Store in the absence of the Campus Store manager and/or during special events. - Assist with other projects and perform other duties as assigned by the Vice President of Marketing and Communications. Skills Needed: - Must be comfortable with Microsoft Office, including Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. - Must have strong interpersonal, customer service, written communication and proofreading skills. - Budget administration experience preferred. Key interfaces: - Works with staff from every campus division, including Executive Leadership Team offices, directors, administrative assistants, faculty, and committee representatives. Also interfaces with Board of Trustee members, external consultants, vendors, and members of the news media. Education & Experience: EITHER - High school diploma and a minimum of five years of experience in a similar position. Experience in educational setting is preferred. OR - Bachelor\u2019s degree and at least three years of experience. - Some specialized training or experience may be required. Working conditions & physical demands: - General office setting with a moderate noise level. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 1e540852 Last Name (required) 6264e490 Email (required) 1311664c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 53f61f6b Last Name (required) 458c46c4 Email (required) 367d75be Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/clinical-educator-in-dietetics-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Clinical Educator in Dietetics", "description": "Clinical Educator in Dietetics - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Clinical Educator in Dietetics - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Clinical Educator in Dietetics 492547 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Faculty Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Meredith College seeks qualified applicants for the position of Clinical Educator in Dietetics. This position is a full-time, eleven-month, instructor of professional practice, faculty appointment. Duties: - Eighteen to twenty-one credit hour teaching load of DI and MSN supervised experiential learning and/or didactic coursework. - Work both in designated hospital location(s) and on the Meredith College campus each week to educate students one-on-one or in small groups, both formally and informally. - Precept dietetic interns and graduate students on a rotating schedule in cohorts at one designated hospital location in Medical Nutrition Therapy/Clinical Nutrition. - Collaborate with the Program Director, hospital managers, and other community partners to plan and implement students\u2019 schedules. - Fulfill all nutrition competencies as required by the hospital. - Model evidence-based practice, professional behavior, time management, and ethical practice. - Assist interns and students in setting appropriate goals and schedules for completing competencies during the rotation. - Identify and facilitate learning activities that support competencies/learning outcomes. - Evaluate each intern/student's progress and provide timely formative feedback to students on strengths and opportunities for growth regarding their provision of Medical Nutrition Therapy and overall professionalism. - Develop and lead campus-based clinical simulations and other alternate learning experiences in the Simulation Lab. - Complete required supervised practice documentation in a timely manner. - Collaborate regularly with the Program Director regarding student performance in supervised experiential learning sites, complete required documentation in a timely manner, and provide remediation when needed. - Assist in development of programmatic materials including preceptor education materials, supervised experiential learning list of required learning activities, rubrics, and authentic simulations, and marketing materials. - Collect and assess data to meet ACEND accreditation requirements. - Participate in the application review and selection process for program candidates. - Attend staff meetings at the hospital and college. - Perform other miscellaneous tasks within the graduate office as identified by the Program Director and/or Department Chair. Qualifications: - Master\u2019s degree in Nutrition Science, Dietetics, or Public Health. Credentialed by CDR as an active Registered Dietitian. - At least three years of clinical nutrition experience is required. - The successful candidate will provide evidence of initiative, maturity, professionalism, attention to detail, excellent organizational ability, time management, and interpersonal skills, which include high-quality oral and written communication skills. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. To apply: submit your letter of interest, vita, teaching philosophy, copy of all transcripts, RD registration number, and list of references with contact information. Official transcripts are required upon hire. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume/CV - Teaching Philosophy - Copy of Transcripts - RD Registration Number - References (within the application) Apply Now! First Name (required) 35ddb1f1 Last Name (required) b4f911d1 Email (required) 92966683 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 3902cecc Last Name (required) da6451eb Email (required) 40dce0ef Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/dietetics-educator-and-dietetic-internship-program-director-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director", "description": "Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director 492546 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Faculty Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Meredith College seeks qualified applicants for the position of Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director. This position is a full-time, eleven-month, faculty appointment. Duties: Teaching responsibilities include on-campus undergraduate and graduate courses in Food and Nutrition. Expertise to teach a variety of food and nutrition courses at Undergraduate and Graduate levels. Serve as Program Director for ACEND accredited Dietetic Internship program and oversee supervised experiential learning. Active involvement within the department; student advising; DI program documentation and administration; scholarship and service to the profession expected. Qualifications: - Master\u2019s degree in Nutrition Sciences, Dietetics, or Public Health. - RD credential with at least five years of professional experience required. - The successful candidate will provide evidence of initiative, maturity, professionalism, attention to detail, excellent organizational ability, time management and interpersonal skills, which include high-quality oral and written communication skills. - Demonstrated or potential excellence in undergraduate & graduate teaching. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. To apply: complete the online application, submit your letter of interest, vita, teaching philosophy, copy of all transcripts, RD registration number, and list of references with contact information. Official transcripts are required upon hire. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume/CV - Teaching Philosophy - Copy of Transcripts - RD Registration Number - References (within the application) Apply Now! First Name (required) c285bf86 Last Name (required) 8a22f45e Email (required) 0bfadfa7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 865c8625 Last Name (required) 2f3788cc Email (required) 1c3c05ef Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/associate-director-of-admissions-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Associate Director of Admissions", "description": "Associate Director of Admissions - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Associate Director of Admissions - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Associate Director of Admissions 492545 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Associate Director serves as a member of the admissions team that serves transfer, WINGS and graduate students. The Associate Director is responsible for assisting in the development and implementation of strategies to recruit, select, and enroll a diverse student body to meet college enrollment targets. The Associate Director will manage an assigned territory consisting of academic programs that serve adult and graduate populations. The Associate Director of Admissions should possess characteristics indicative of a strong collaborative leader: integrity, intellect, work ethic, initiative, creativity, flexibility, and enthusiasm for the work. Skills important for success in this position include excellent public speaking skills, strong writing skills, planning and problem-solving, interpreting data to inform and enhance recruitment strategies, and strong relationship-building and supervisory ability. Duties: - Meet enrollment goals for assigned academic area(s) by representing Meredith at community college visits, community events, working one-on-one with families during on-campus visits, while meeting or exceeding weekly outreach requirements for students across the admissions funnel - Serve as the primary liaison between admissions unit and department heads, faculty and Deans for assigned academic programs - Review applications and offer decisions on behalf of the college based on admissions criteria set by the program and/or college - Collaborate with the admission office leadership team to develop practices that enhance productivity and streamline application, admission, and enrollment processes - Responsibility for coordinating one or more recruiting events and assisting with other events as needed - Monitor and control costs of recruitment travel, and produce follow-up reports for the effectiveness of travel - Develop relationships with other college departments and key secondary school constituents to enhance customer service and satisfaction - Represent the Office of Admissions in a public-speaking capacity on and off campus and maintain records of these activities - Collaborate with campus constituents to develop and implement selected recruitment and pre-orientation events - Serve on College committees as assigned - Perform other related duties as needed or assigned Skills Needed: - Must have excellent interpersonal skills and be able to work with a diverse community - Ability to effectively communicate in person, via phone, and in writing and make effective public presentations - Strong relationship-building skills - Thorough understanding of College procedures, curricular offerings, student outcomes, and be able to relate this information effectively to prospective students and families - Must be able to understand and explain financial aid programs, eligibility criteria, and award procedures - Ability to interpret and apply data to decision-making - Ability to maintain an effective applicant tracking system - Strong planning and organization capabilities - Excellent time management and attention to detail Key interfaces: - Interacts with prospective students, families, and community college liaisons - Outreach and partnerships with local businesses and organizations - Office of Admission staff, and members of the Meredith community Education & Experience: - Master\u2019s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience required - Minimum of three - five years admissions and recruiting experience or related work - Valid NC Driver\u2019s license required and clear driving history Working conditions & physical demands: - General office setting with moderate noise level - Frequent travel required - Evening and Weekend work required Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) b6178aab Last Name (required) 7bcbd3f8 Email (required) b569eaea Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 485d0617 Last Name (required) 843cdfa6 Email (required) b8e6a563 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/adjunct-faculty-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty", "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty 492541 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Adjunct Instructor Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Meredith college seeks qualified professionals for adjunct teaching positions for undergraduate and graduate courses in a variety of disciplines. Meredith College is a women\u2019s institution for first-time traditional women college students, transfer students, adult degree completers, and both male and female graduate students. Built-in comprehensive coaching and advising are provided throughout the undergraduate experience to ensure students are supported and positioned for success. We are looking for adjunct faculty for the following disciplines: Business Administration (marketing, supply chain, data analytics, operations), Biology (anatomy and physiology, genetics), Chemistry, Computer Science, Criminal Justice, Data Analytics, History, Mathematics, Psychology, Political Science, Social Work, Statistics, French and Spanish. Qualifications: Education/Experience: - To be considered for a position in our applicant pool, applicants are required to possess a graduate (terminal) degree in the relevant field with a minimum of 18 graduate hours from an accredited university. - In addition to the graduate degree, expertise in teaching the subject matter is desired. - All graduate work must be documented with official transcripts submitted to the university upon request. - Teaching experience in traditional and/or online education is desired. - Experience working with either Brightspace or Canvas learning management systems is desired. Knowledge, Skills, And Abilities: - Communicate effectively to all groups through both oral and written channels. - Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint and the Internet. Application Instructions: Please include the following with your application: - Curriculum Vitae, required - Cover letter - Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts for all related degrees, licenses/certificates will be required upon hire) Optional Additional Attachments: - Teaching Philosophy - Sample Syllabus - Additional Licenses/Certifications - Course Evaluations Apply Now! First Name (required) 30ef0c8a Last Name (required) bf262798 Email (required) 5a710178 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) f1a89ab6 Last Name (required) 39bdfa09 Email (required) 7058120b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/security-officer-part-time-flexible-schedule-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Security Officer, Part-time (Flexible Schedule)", "description": "Security Officer, Part-time (Flexible Schedule) - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Security Officer, Part-time (Flexible Schedule) - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Security Officer, Part-time (Flexible Schedule) 492501 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Part-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Provides safety and security services to students, staff, faculty, and visitors through efficient use of departmental resources. Position is classified as essential personnel under college policy and is subject to college and department policies regarding essential personnel. Performs essential duties related to security work as identified by management during inclement weather, emergency situations, or as campus needs dictate. Position may require shift, weekend, and/or overtime work. Seeking applicants with maximum flexibility and the ability to be available on a call-in status. There are no guarantees on the number of hours per week. The position will fill in for vacation periods as well as work during holidays throughout the year. This position is less than 1,000 hours per year and is not eligible for benefits. First Shift hours: 7am \u2013 3pm; Second Shift hours: 3pm \u2013 11pm; Third Shift hours: 11pm \u2013 7am. Duties : - Responds to all calls for service and request for assistance from Meredith College student, staff, faculty and visitors. - Determines necessary and appropriate actions needed to resolve problems and answers calls for service. May need to resort to applying minimum levels of force at times. - Patrols campus by vehicle or foot. Controls access to campus and the Greenway during closing hours. - Responds to any call, fire or intrusion alarms, including suspicious person(s) and take appropriate action. - Provides traffic direction for large and small events. - Enforces parking regulations, including towing and auto-booting as appropriate. Provides car unlock, jump start, and other automotive services to students, faculty, and staff. (Flat tires can be changed if the conditions are safe). - Checks doors and window of building to ensure they are secure. Turns on and turn off interior and exterior light according to set schedules or special request. - Duties may include inclement weather safety responsibilities as necessary due to inclement weather and activities related to emergency situations. - May be required to work during campus closures. - Assist in turning on and off campus lighting for Special Events and scheduled sports activities. Skills Needed: - Ability to use discretion in handling difficult persons and analyze situations likely to be encountered on patrol. - Observe and retain names, faces and details of occurrences; keep detailed notes for report writing and other daily log sheets, understand and correct emergency alarm systems. - Observe legal and defensive driving practices; interpret, apply and explain rules, regulations, policies and procedures. - Ability to understand and work within the scope of authority; apply policies and procedures. Key interfaces: - Responds to calls by students, faculty, staff and visitors. - May need to confront hostile or belligerent persons in an appropriate and professional manner. Education & Experience : - High School Diploma or equivalent required. - Current NC Driver License and clear driving history. - Previous security experience is a plus Working conditions & physical demands: - Position may require shift, weekend, and/or overtime work. Seeking applicants with maximum flexibility and the ability to be available on a call-in status. There are no guarantees on the number of hours per week. The position will fill in for vacation periods as well as work during holidays throughout the year. This position is less than 1,000 hours per year and is not eligible for benefits. - Must be able to work any shift and respond/report for duty, as necessary. Part of duties may include general office setting with moderate noise level. Must be able to operate company vehicles. - Patrols campus outdoors and may be exposed to the weather. May be held for additional shifts during inclement weather, if relief is not possible. - Ability to navigate physical obstacles, such as walls, heights, etc. Ability to physically help students, faculty, and staff having health issues. - Must be able to walk for extended distances, stand for long periods, climb stairs, and run, as necessary. - Must occasionally lift up to 50 lbs. Apply Now! First Name (required) 30eeb5de Last Name (required) 3db46828 Email (required) 571e67f5 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 7cea3604 Last Name (required) e187fa36 Email (required) 7e6dda35 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/adjunct-instructor-of-genetics-and-or-human-anatomy-physiology-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology", "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Adjunct Instructor of Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Instructor of Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology 492540 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Adjunct Instructor Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Biology Department at Meredith College invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to teach lecture and laboratory courses in Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology beginning Fall 2026. We seek colleagues committed to high quality undergraduate teaching, and supporting student success in a liberal arts environment. Responsibilities: - Teach lecture and/or laboratory sections in Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology - Develop and deliver course materials that align with departmental learning outcomes - Provide timely assessment, feedback, and academic support to students - Maintain clear communication with department leadership - Uphold all instructional, safety, and compliance standards for laboratory teaching Minimum Qualifications: - Master\u2019s degree in Biology, Genetics, Physiology, or a closely related discipline - Demonstrated experience teaching undergraduate students or evidence of strong potential for effective instruction - Commitment to fostering a supportive learning environment Application Materials: \u2022 Cover letter describing teaching experience and areas of expertise \u2022 Curriculum vitae \u2022 Contact information for at least two professional references \u2022 (Optional) Sample syllabus or evidence of teaching effectiveness Appointment Details: Adjunct appointments are semester based and part time. Compensation is commensurate with qualifications and course load. Opportunities for continued teaching may be available based on departmental needs. How to Apply: Complete the online application. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until positions are filled. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume / CV - References (within the application) Apply Now! First Name (required) ee2372dc Last Name (required) 0536e427 Email (required) 42b34c70 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) bd03f559 Last Name (required) b9cd1787 Email (required) 0bc9c24f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/director-of-career-planning-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Director of Career Planning", "description": "Director of Career Planning - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Director of Career Planning - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Director of Career Planning 492529 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Director of Career Planning provides strategic leadership for a comprehensive, outcomes-driven career development program that supports students and alumnae in achieving meaningful post-graduate success. This role is responsible for aligning career services with the mission of the College and advancing institutional priorities related to student success, retention, and career outcomes. The Director leads the development of innovative programs, employer partnerships, and campus collaborations that integrate career readiness throughout the student experience. Through data-informed decision-making, technology integration, and a commitment to equitable access, the Director enables students to be prepared to navigate a dynamic and evolving workforce. The Director provides strategic leadership, supervision, and professional development for Career Planning staff, fostering a collaborative, high-performing team accountable for achieving student career outcomes and delivering innovative, student-centered services. Duties: Strategic Leadership & Career Outcomes - Develop and implement a comprehensive, data-informed career services strategy aligned with College\u2019s Strategic Plan and Institutional Goals - Represent the College and collaborate with campus partners to advance institutional priorities related to student recruitment, retention, and graduation, including leveraging career outcomes and programming to support student success - Leverage career outcomes data and programming to strengthen the College\u2019s value proposition for prospective and current students - Establish, monitor, and report student first destination career outcomes - Lead departmental program assessment efforts, including continuous improvement plans and reports, comprehensive program assessments, and other outcome measures, to evaluate program effectiveness and inform continuous improvement - Utilize data analytics and labor market insights to guide strategic priorities and resource allocation Employer & External Relations - Develop and execute a proactive employer engagement strategy to expand internships, job opportunities, and experiential learning partnerships - Cultivate and maintain relationships with local, regional, and national employers, as well as alumnae and industry partners - Collaborate with Institutional Advancement and Alumnae Relations to strengthen employer and mentoring networks - Represent the College to external stakeholders and enhance the institution\u2019s visibility and reputation among employers Student Career Development & Readiness - Oversee the design and delivery of a comprehensive career development model that equips students with essential career readiness competencies - Ensure equitable access to high-impact practices such as internships, networking opportunities, and career counseling - Provide career counseling to students and alumnae, including administering and interpreting career assessments - Lead workshops, classroom presentations, and programming on career and professional development topics Campus Collaboration & Curriculum Integration - Partner with faculty and academic departments to integrate career development into the curriculum - Work collaboratively across campus to ensure students can effectively translate their academic, leadership, and experiential learning into clear, confident career pathways - Collaborate across campus to embed career readiness into the student experience, including first-year through senior year initiatives - Support the development of experiential learning opportunities, including internships and applied learning experiences - Serve on institutional committees related to student success, retention, and strategic planning Technology, Innovation & Operations - Oversee the implementation and optimization of career services technology platforms (e.g., career management systems - Handshake, assessment tools) - Integrate emerging technologies, including AI, to enhance career education, coaching, and operational efficiency - Ensure students are prepared to ethically and effectively use technology in the job search process - Develop and manage departmental policies, procedures, and annual budget Marketing, Outreach & Engagement - Lead a strategic communication plan to promote career services programs, resources, and outcomes - Increase student engagement and utilization of career services across all class years - Promote career success stories and outcomes to internal and external audiences Supervision & Staff Development - Supervise, mentor, and evaluate team members through regular meetings, professional development, and performance reviews - Foster a collaborative, innovative, and student-centered team culture - Train and supervise graduate student interns Access & Inclusion - Develop and implement strategies to promote equitable career outcomes for all students - Identify and address gaps in access to career opportunities and resources - Partner with campus stakeholders and employers to advance inclusive hiring practices Additional Responsibilities: - Serve as a member of Campus Committees, including the StrongPoints Advisory Committee - Maintain active participation in professional organizations and remain current on trends and best practices in career services Skills Needed: - Strategic thinking, leadership, and management skills with the ability to drive innovation and change - Strong relationship-building and collaboration skills with internal and external stakeholders - Expertise in career counseling, coaching, and student development - Ability to analyze and utilize data to inform decisions and demonstrate impact - Familiarity with career services technology platforms and emerging tools, including AI - Excellent communication, presentation, and storytelling skills - Commitment to fostering inclusive and equitable student outcomes Key Interfaces: - Interacts extensively with college administrators, faculty, and staff - Engages with students, faculty & staff, alumnae, employers, families, and community partners - Represents the College on campus and in external professional and employer communities Education, Experience, Certifications: - Master\u2019s degree in counseling, student development, higher education administration, or a related field - Professional certifications such as career counseling/coaching credentials, assessment certifications, or leadership/HR certifications (e.g., NACE, NCDA, SHRM, Gallup Strengths Coaching) are preferred - Significant experience in career services, career development, or a related field - Demonstrated leadership experience, including supervision and program management - Experience with assessment, data analysis, and program evaluation - Proven success in building employer partnerships and external relationships preferred Working Conditions & Physical Demands: - General office setting with moderate noise - Occasional evening and weekend work, as well as travel, may be required - Valid NC Driver's License and clear driving history required. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Please note that the search timeline for this position has been extended pending the appointment of our new Vice President for Student Affairs, who will participate in the selection process. We encourage interested candidates to continue applying and appreciate your patience as we move through this important leadership transition. Apply Now! First Name (required) 3db400c0 Last Name (required) 32ea2f9a Email (required) b91c921c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 4ff6ad90 Last Name (required) c694f6c1 Email (required) 0be5569d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/groundskeeper-irrigation-technician-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Groundskeeper / Irrigation Technician", "description": "Groundskeeper / Irrigation Technician - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Groundskeeper / Irrigation Technician - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Groundskeeper / Irrigation Technician 492536 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Position is responsible for providing technical support, skills and labor towards the routine care and maintenance of a clean, beautiful and safe campus environment. Works in concert with the grounds team to maintain and enhance the function and aesthetics of the campus grounds. Position is classified as essential personnel under college policy and is subject to college and department policies regarding essential personnel. Performs essential duties as identified by management and incident response team related to inclement or hazardous weather events. Duties: - Leads in the operation, maintenance and repair of campus irrigation systems and pump stations. - Operates heavy equipment including zero turn mowers, articulating tractor, skid steer tractor, farm tractor, and large area mowers in the routine completion grounds maintenance tasks. - Routinely clears sidewalks, entrances, courtyards, campus roads and parking lots of debris using tractor with hydraulic high-powered blower. - Performs routine lawn and landscape maintenance including mowing edging, weeding, tree and shrub pruning - Routinely clears of sidewalks, entrances, courtyards, campus roads and parking lots using tractor with hydraulic high-powered blower. - Routinely collects and properly disposes of litter, trash, organic debris and recyclables in assigned areas. - Assists in the routine maintenance of athletic fields and facilities. - Assists in the repair of brick sidewalks, road signs, parking lots and campus roads surfaces. - Performs snow and storm related campus clean up, removing debris and snow from sidewalks, parking lots, and building entrances to ensure safe conditions for students, faculty and staff. - Duties may include activities related to preparation or clean-up during emergency situations. - May be required to work during campus closures. - Performs other related duties as necessary or as assigned by supervisor. Skills Needed: - Must be able to effectively communicate, verbally and in writing, with supervisor, coworkers, customers and others. - Must be highly skilled in the operation of grounds powered equipment and heavy machinery including the safe operation of: skid steer, tractor, articulating tractor, backhoe, hydraulic leaf blower reel mower, zero turn mower, snow broom and snow plow. - Must be highly skilled in the performance of grounds maintenance tasks such as mowing, edging, string-trimming, hedge-trimming, leaf and trash removal. - Must have knowledge of irrigation system repair and installation. - Must be highly skilled in the repair and maintenance of irrigation pump stations, controllers, solenoid valves and sprinkler heads. Key Interfaces: - Will work closely with Grounds Supervisor and other Grounds Staff. Education, Experience, Certifications: - High school diploma or GED preferred. - Must have irrigation repair and installation experience. - Grounds and landscape maintenance experience is required. - Valid NC Driver's License and clear driving history is required. Working conditions & physical demands: - The nature of the working environment may produce moderate levels of stress and involves discomfort and/or risk such as operating gas-powered equipment, heavy machinery and dangerous cutting equipment. - Workers are subject to environmental discomfort such as frequent exposure to loud noises, and/or extremes of heat or cold. - The work frequently requires wearing protective gear that may be uncomfortable. - Must be able to perform strenuous work that involves frequent exertion and/or periods of continuous machine operation. - Frequent lifting of objects over 50 pounds. Occasional lifting of heavy objects weighing 75 pounds or more is required. - Frequent standing and operating machinery. - May be required to work during periods of inclement weather. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 7c6930b4 Last Name (required) 2b9bf8d8 Email (required) 78b30d0a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 0080d84b Last Name (required) ae21e363 Email (required) cd79de63 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/chair-school-of-business-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Chair - School of Business", "description": "Chair - School of Business - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Chair - School of Business - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Chair - School of Business 492534 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Administrative Faculty / Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Meredith College is seeking a chair for the Business Department. Chairs at Meredith are faculty leaders responsible for overseeing academic quality, curriculum alignment, faculty performance, and operations. The Business Department offers a bachelor\u2019s degree in business administration with concentrations in accounting, marketing, hospitality and tourism, and degrees in economics, and a minor in finance. The department also offers an MBA degree. Responsibilities: Department Curriculum - Oversee curriculum development and revisions for the department - Review and assess academic programs offered by the department - Assess general education outcomes in core courses taught within the department - Initiate new academic programs and projects when appropriate Department Operations - Manage course schedules that serve program and student needs - Manage course registrations and instructor assignments - Oversee the department's fiscal operations; develop and regularly monitor the department budget - Review and revise department information published in the college catalog - Manage the maintenance of departmental print and electronic records, including websites Personnel - Recruit, appoint, and supervise faculty in conjunction with the provost - Evaluate faculty and staff performance - Support and oversee the overall development of the department faculty and staff - Recruit, appoint, and supervise department staff and student assistants - Review faculty and staff grievances within the department Students - Recruit and retain students in the department's programs - Coordinate student advising and reviews of degree progress - Evaluate student transfer credit - Review student academic appeals and grievances Faculty Responsibilities - Teach at least two classes per semester - Participate in research and scholarly activities in the discipline - Participate and assist department faculty in college and community service activities as appropriate Required skills and experiences: - In-depth understanding of academic policies, curriculum development, and accreditation processes - Strong leadership and organizational skills, with the ability to manage budgets and personnel effectively - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills - Proven ability to support faculty research, student success initiatives, and community engagement - Demonstrated competency in data-driven decision-making Essential Job Functions: - Provide academic leadership for all programs within the department - Oversee budget development and resource allocation to support college and departmental goals and priorities - Recruit, mentor, and evaluate faculty and staff while promoting professional development - Lead efforts to assess and enhance academic programs, including accreditation and program review - Other related duties, as assigned Qualifications: An earned doctorate or terminal degree in a business; preference given to specialty area in strategic management, marketing, or economics. Required Documents: - Resume / CV - Cover Letter Apply Now! First Name (required) 5e47c97a Last Name (required) d650058c Email (required) b023b8d8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 683ea7d9 Last Name (required) 442c087e Email (required) 2e226455 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/maintenance-technician-iii-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Maintenance Technician III", "description": "Maintenance Technician III - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Maintenance Technician III - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Maintenance Technician III 492526 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Maintenance Technician III is the senior technical role in the Facilities Services maintenance department. This position performs advanced maintenance, repair, installation, and preventive maintenance work across multiple trade areas with full independence, and carries significant leadership responsibility for the quality, safety, and development of the maintenance team. The Maintenance Technician III serves as the primary technical authority in the department, mentors and trains Technician I, Technician II, and Facilities Maintenance Assistant staff, and functions as lead worker in the absence of the Maintenance Supervisor. This role is the direct step up from Maintenance Technician II and the primary advancement path toward the Maintenance Supervisor role. This position is classified as essential personnel under College policy and participates in an on-call rotation for after-hours and emergency response. Duties: - Performs advanced routine, corrective, project, and preventive maintenance work across multiple trade areas \u2014 including plumbing, carpentry, painting, plastering, electrical, and machine servicing. - Diagnoses maintenance problems, determines appropriate repair approaches, and completes repairs to a high standard of workmanship. - Serves as lead worker in the absence of the Maintenance Supervisor \u2014 coordinates daily work assignments, serves as the primary point of contact for urgent work orders, and ensures work quality across the team. - Provides formal on-the-job mentorship, technical coaching, and skills development guidance to Maintenance Technician I, Technician II, and Facilities Maintenance Assistant staff. - Reviews and evaluates the quality of completed work by junior staff on shared or sequential projects; communicates quality concerns to the Maintenance Supervisor. - Contributes to the formal skills assessment of junior staff as requested by the supervisor. - Leads small renovation and repair projects from initial diagnosis through completion, including planning, material estimation, and workmanship oversight. - Estimates time and material costs of assigned projects independently; communicates material and parts needs to the inventory controller or purchasing staff. - Reads, interprets, and works from architectural drawings, engineering schematics, equipment manuals, and manufacturer documentation independently. - Participates in the hiring process for junior positions at the supervisor's request, including reviewing applications and participating in candidate interviews. - Inspects completed repairs and installations to verify proper operation, safety, workmanship, and cleanliness. - Maintains tools, equipment, vehicles, and work areas in a clean, organized, and safe condition. - Performs all work in accordance with established safety procedures, applicable codes, OSHA standards, and college policies. - Interacts professionally and courteously with students, faculty, staff, contractors, and visitors while working in occupied buildings and active campus environments. - Participates in the department's on-call rotation and responds, as assigned, to after-hours, weekend, holiday, and emergency maintenance needs. - Assists with inclement weather response, emergency response, and other campus support work as directed. - Performs other related duties as assigned. Qualifications: - High school diploma or GED required; completion of a formal trade apprenticeship or vocational program preferred. - Five or more years of progressively responsible experience in building maintenance, facilities maintenance, or related maintenance trades required, with demonstrated advanced competency across multiple trade areas. - Demonstrated experience performing advanced maintenance and repair work independently across a minimum of two trade areas. - Ability to read, interpret, and work from architectural drawings, engineering schematics, and manufacturer documentation independently. - Demonstrated ability to estimate project costs and plan multi-step repair and installation projects without supervisor input. - Demonstrated ability or willingness to mentor and develop less experienced staff. - Ability to communicate effectively in English. - Ability to work independently with minimal supervision and to coordinate the work of others as a lead worker. - Ability and willingness to participate in an on-call rotation and respond to campus as required for urgent or emergency situations. - Valid NC driver's license and acceptable driving record. - Experience using a computerized maintenance management system or work order system preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: - Advanced working knowledge of two or more building trade areas including plumbing, carpentry, painting/plastering, minor electrical, and general mechanical systems. - Ability to independently diagnose, plan, and execute complex maintenance repairs and installations across multiple trade areas. - Strong leadership, mentoring, and coaching skills; ability to coordinate the work of others and model professional standards for the team. - Working knowledge of applicable OSHA safety standards, safe work practices, and building codes relevant to maintenance trade work. - Skill in reading and working from architectural drawings, engineering schematics, and complex technical documentation. - Ability to estimate project materials and labor requirements accurately and independently. - Ability to prioritize work, manage time efficiently, and adapt to changing campus needs and daily assignments. - Ability to demonstrate dependability, professionalism, accountability, flexibility, and customer service in a service-oriented environment. - Effective written and verbal communication skills; ability to document work thoroughly and provide clear technical direction to junior staff. Physical Demands: - Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and frequently lift or carry objects weighing up to 25 pounds. - Frequent bending, reaching, climbing, walking, standing, kneeling, pushing, and pulling. - Ability to work from ladders and aerial lift equipment including boom lifts and scissor lifts as required. MEWP operator training is provided. - May be exposed to heat, cold, dust, noise, moisture, and other conditions typical of facilities maintenance work. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 21ae26e5 Last Name (required) c9302f71 Email (required) 69241fef Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) c6bd3059 Last Name (required) be828188 Email (required) b384fc33 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/maintenance-technician-ii-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Maintenance Technician II", "description": "Maintenance Technician II - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Maintenance Technician II - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Maintenance Technician II 492525 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Maintenance Technician II performs general maintenance, repair, installation, and preventive maintenance work in support of campus buildings, systems, equipment, and related spaces. This hands-on role supports residence halls, academic buildings, administrative spaces, and other campus operations and is suited for someone who is dependable, adaptable, and comfortable handling a broad range of maintenance needs. This position is classified as essential personnel under College policy and participates in an on-call rotation for after-hours and emergency response. Duties: - Performs routine, corrective, project, and preventive maintenance work as assigned. - Responds to work orders, service requests, and urgent maintenance needs in a timely, professional, and efficient manner. - Performs a variety of general building maintenance and repair tasks, including plumbing, carpentry, painting, wall and ceiling repair, hardware repairs, fixture replacement, basic electrical troubleshooting, and other general maintenance duties within skill level and training. - Troubleshoots maintenance problems and identifies repair or follow-up needs. - Inspects buildings, rooms, equipment, fixtures, and building components to identify maintenance and preventive maintenance needs. - Documents completed work, labor, materials used, and follow-up needs in the College's maintenance management system. - Maintains tools, equipment, vehicles, and work areas in a clean, organized, and safe condition. - Performs all work in accordance with established safety practices and departmental expectations. - Interacts professionally and courteously with students, faculty, staff, contractors, and visitors while working in occupied buildings and active campus environments. - Participates in the department's on-call rotation and responds, as assigned, to after-hours, weekend, holiday, and emergency maintenance needs. - Assists with inclement weather response, emergency response, and other campus support work as directed. - Performs other related duties as assigned. Qualifications: - High school diploma or equivalent preferred. - One to two years of hands-on experience in building maintenance, facilities, property maintenance, construction, or a closely related trade required. Candidates with apartment, hotel, commercial, or institutional maintenance experience are encouraged to apply. - Experience performing a broad range of general maintenance and repair work in occupied facilities preferred. - Demonstrated experience in one or more of the following trade areas: general building maintenance and repair; basic plumbing; carpentry; painting and wall repair; basic electrical; or general mechanical/equipment repair. - Ability to read and follow work orders, equipment manuals, diagrams, labels, and written instructions. - Ability to communicate effectively in English. - Ability to work independently with limited supervision and also function effectively as part of a team. - Ability and willingness to participate in an on-call rotation and respond to campus as required for urgent or emergency situations. - Valid NC driver's license and acceptable driving record. - Experience using a computerized maintenance management system or work order system preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: - Working knowledge of tools, materials, methods, and safety practices used in general building maintenance. - Ability to perform a broad range of maintenance and repair work within skill level and training. - Ability to troubleshoot common building-related problems and complete repairs safely and effectively. - Ability to prioritize work, manage time efficiently, and adapt to changing campus needs and daily assignments. - Ability to demonstrate dependability, professionalism, flexibility, and customer service in a service-oriented environment. - Ability to work effectively in occupied buildings and maintain productive working relationships with others in a campus setting. Physical Demands: - Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and frequently lift or carry objects weighing up to 25 pounds. - Frequent bending, reaching, climbing, walking, standing, kneeling, pushing, and pulling. - Ability to work from ladders and aerial lift equipment including boom lifts and scissor lifts as required. MEWP operator training is provided. - May be exposed to heat, cold, dust, noise, moisture, and other conditions typical of facilities maintenance work. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) af8fe8df Last Name (required) 8e36a713 Email (required) a952318e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 8a61efde Last Name (required) 8091764a Email (required) 2eb9d28f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-director-of-financial-assistance-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Director of Financial Assistance", "description": "Assistant Director of Financial Assistance - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Assistant Director of Financial Assistance - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Director of Financial Assistance 492517 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. General Purpose of Position Assists in administering need-based and non-need-based federal, state, private, and institutional financial assistance programs and ensures compliance with all federal, state, and institutional policies. Essential Duties & Responsibilities: -Manage and work with Institutional Advancement, regarding the underwriting of Institutional Endowed scholarships and awards -Monitor students regarding their satisfactory academic progress in federal aid programs -Monitor students to ensure student recipients remain in good standing regarding their specific institutional scholarship fund. -Counsel, verify, package, and award both prospective and upper class students -Serve as primary FA Counselor for those studying abroad -Performs other duties as assigned Skills Needed: -Experience working with Microsoft Office, including Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, Excel and the ability to work with mainframe database systems. -Experienced in providing customer service -Proficient written and oral communications skills -Excellent interpersonal skills Key interfaces: -Interaction with continuing students, prospective students, faculty, and staff of the college -Interaction with Federal and State officials -Interaction with student loan agencies Education & Experience: -Bachelor\u2019s Degree required, master degree preferred -At least three years experience in financial assistance and/or significant work experience. Working conditions & physical demands -General office setting with moderate noise level Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume/CV Apply Now! First Name (required) 2d7399ed Last Name (required) 9a84cd73 Email (required) bc782855 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) dc07efa4 Last Name (required) 5b9c41fd Email (required) e159d486 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Candidate Details"}, "https://www.meredith.edu/faculty-staff/": {"title": "Faculty & Staff - Meredith College", "description": "Faculty & Staff - Meredith College Faculty & Staff - Meredith College Brightspace Email Emergency Handbook MyMeredith People Registrar Self Service Faculty & Staff Whether you\u2019re a new faculty or staff member at Meredith, or getting ready to retire, you\u2019ve come to the right place. Here you\u2019ll find everything you need to keep going strong. Main Line : (919) 760-8600 Campus Police : (919) 760-8888 Employment : (919) 760-8898 Registrar : (919) 760-8593 Facilities : (919) 760-8560 Health Services : (919) 760-8535 Supply Store : (919) 760-8545 Employee Resources Accessibility at Meredith Accounting CamCards Campus Police College Lectures Dining Emergency Planning Facilities Services Giving to Meredith Health & Human Performance Lab Human Resources Marketing Postal Services Research, Planning & Assessment Technology Services Wellness Staff Information First Year Experience MyMeredith Self Service Faculty Information Academic Advising Assessments Catalogues Faculty Development First Year Experience General Education Graduate Handbook Helping Students in Academic Difficulty Honors Colloquia Registrar Undergraduate Handbook Research The following links are in PDF format. IRB Guidelines IRB Application Consent Waiver Addendum Modification Form Renewal-Closure Form Adverse Event Report News Headlines Registration Open for 28th Annual Meredith College Golf Classic Study Abroad + Away Program Applications Open Faculty/Staff Accomplishments 10/14/26 Ceremony Held to Unveil Historical Marker Proposed by Meredith Students Meredith to Hold Event Honoring Women Veterans on November 11 Upcoming Events Oct 7 Oct 12 Oct 15 Oct 15 Oct 15 Oct 15 Oct 15 Oct 16 View Calendar"}, "https://www.meredith.edu/employers-career-planning/": {"title": "Career Planning: Employers - Meredith College", "description": "Career Planning: Employers - Meredith College Career Planning: Employers - Meredith College Career Planning: Employers Engage with Meredith Students Post a Position FAQs Hiring International Students Employer Recruiting Opportunities Internships Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Staff Meredith College welcomes the opportunity to work with you and your organization as you seek students, recent graduates and experienced alumnae for internships, co-ops, and full-time career opportunities. Please contact Mackenzie Bradley, Career Planning Program Coordinator, at mrbradley@meredith.edu to learn more about upcoming opportunities to meet Meredith students and how to build a recruiting partnership. Find Meredith students on Handshake! The Office of Career Planning is excited to welcome you to Handshake, a one-stop platform to manage all of your on- and off-campus recruiting needs, share and update job postings, connect with students, and more. All organizations recruiting at Meredith College must adhere to the Meredith College Recruiting Guidelines . Please note: employers and positions are vetted by our team before being posted. Helpful Handshake Resources: Register for an Employer Account Connect with Meredith College Approve Staff Members Questions? Contact support@joinhandshake.com Interested in hiring a part-time tutor, teacher, or nanny? The Office of Financial Assistance hosts a job board for part-time positions. Please complete and return their employment form to finaid@meredith.edu . Office of Career Planning Contact Information Mackenzie Bradley Career Planning Program Coordinator 205 Park Center (919) 760-8343 mrbradley@meredith.edu"}}, "rows": {"https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/search": {"school_id": 805, "posting_url": "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/search", "job_title_in_post": "Search Page", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Business", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.meredith.edu/human-resources/applying-for-a-position/": {"school_id": 805, "posting_url": "https://www.meredith.edu/human-resources/applying-for-a-position/", "job_title_in_post": "Applying for a Position - Meredith College", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/hvac-mechanic-ii-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"school_id": 805, "posting_url": "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/hvac-mechanic-ii-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states", "job_title_in_post": "HVAC Mechanic II", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/hvac-mechanic-i-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {"school_id": 805, "posting_url": "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/hvac-mechanic-i-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states", "job_title_in_post": "HVAC Mechanic I", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/hvac-technician-iii-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states-1b96a69e-b85e-4d1d-9773-ae1aba611a91": {"school_id": 805, "posting_url"